      "Distributor Cap and Rotor Moisture: The traditional distributor cap and ignition rotor are highly susceptible to moisture ingress and carbon tracking. This leads to weak spark delivery, severe misfires under load, and poor fuel economy in wet weather conditions. A high-quality Bosch replacement cap and rotor alongside new ignition leads is required.",
      "Vacuum System Leaks: The Bosch KE-Jetronic system relies heavily on absolute vacuum integrity to meter fuel correctly. The rubber vacuum hoses and the large rubber boot under the air flow meter become brittle and crack, creating massive unmetered air leaks. This results in a fluctuating idle, stalling, and a heavily leaned-out fuel mixture.",
      "Timing Chain Guide Wear: While the duplex timing chain itself is incredibly robust, the plastic guide rails become brittle and snap after thirty years of heat cycling. If a broken guide rail piece falls into the timing cover, it can cause the chain to jump teeth. Preventative replacement of the upper guide rails is highly recommended to protect the valvetrain.",
      "Alternator Voltage Regulator Wear: The carbon brushes inside the alternator voltage regulator wear down over high mileages, preventing the battery from charging. This causes a cascade of low-voltage issues, dimming headlights, and eventual stalling while driving. The regulator is a cheap, easily accessible part that can be swapped without removing the entire alternator."
