    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). A massive upgrade over the M103's single-row chain. The M104 timing chain is virtually bulletproof and rarely stretches or snaps, though the plastic guide rails can still become brittle and crack after 25+ years of heat cycling.",
    "injectionType": "Bosch HFM-SFI (Hot-Film Management Sequential Fuel Injection). A revolutionary leap forward from the antiquated mechanical KE-Jetronic. This fully electronic system utilizes a mass airflow sensor and electronic injectors, providing vastly superior reliability, precise fuel metering, and smooth cold starts.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. Mechanically, the M104 3.2L inline-six is considered one of the greatest engines Mercedes-Benz ever produced, featuring a virtually indestructible cast-iron block. However, the true lifespan of the vehicle is entirely dictated by addressing the catastrophic 'eco-junk' biodegradable wiring harness and the infamous front right head gasket oil leak.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. Delivering a phenomenally smooth, linear 300 Nm torque curve, it completely lacks the complexity and intense thermal stress of turbocharged engines, making it ideal for severe, low-speed off-road abuse.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch HFM (Motronic). A fully modern, highly intelligent engine management unit that allows for precise diagnostics via a 38-pin connector. It responds well to minor chip tuning, but its true advantage lies in replacing the miserable mechanical distributor of previous generations.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 2",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "450+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, massive crankshaft, and cast-iron block are heavily over-engineered. The M104 is legendary in the tuning community, capable of handling immense aftermarket turbo boost on entirely stock internals.",
