    "oilSpecification": "7.0L 10W-40 Fully Synthetic. Strict 10,000 km oil change intervals are mandatory to protect the 24-valve hydraulic lifters and the variable valve timing mechanism on the intake camshaft.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Biodegradable Wiring Harness Degradation: The absolute most devastating flaw of the 1994-1997 era. Mercedes utilized 'eco-friendly' wiring insulation that literally crumbles into dust from engine heat. This exposes bare copper wires, causing massive short circuits that destroy ignition coils and the main ECU. Replacing the entire engine wiring harness is non-negotiable.",
      "Electronic Throttle Actuator (ETA) Failure: The electronic throttle body utilizes the same biodegradable wiring internally. The insulation flakes off, causing the throttle to stick, surge wildly, or trigger Limp Mode (ASR light). The ETA must be completely rebuilt by a specialist.",
      "Head Gasket Oil Leak (Front Right Corner): An extremely famous M104 design flaw. The cylinder head gasket almost universally fails at the front right corner (passenger side) where a high-pressure oil passage is located. It dumps engine oil down the side of the block, requiring a highly labor-intensive head gasket replacement.",
      "Ignition Coil Pack Failure: The M104 utilizes a 'wasted spark' coil-on-plug setup located deep in the valley between the DOHC camshafts. Because of the extreme trapped heat and failing wiring harnesses, these coil packs frequently crack and fail, causing severe misfires under load.",
      "Water Pump Leakage: The mechanical water pump bears the massive load of the viscous fan clutch. The internal bearings wear out, leading to noisy operation and coolant weeping from the weep hole. Immediate replacement is required to prevent the fan from wobbling and shattering the radiator shroud.",
      "OVP Relay / K40 Relay Failures: The Overvoltage Protection (OVP) or K40 relay modules contain cold solder joints that crack over decades of vibration. This causes completely random stalling, rough idling, and illuminated ABS/ASR warning lights on the dashboard."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic ECU Destruction: If the crumbling biodegradable wiring harness is not replaced, the exposed wires will inevitably cross-circuit. Sending 12 volts directly down a 5-volt sensor line will instantly fry the delicate circuit board inside the Bosch ECU, resulting in a financially devastating replacement cost.",
      "Ignition Coil Melt-Down: The degraded wiring harness frequently shorts the ignition coil signal wires directly to ground. This causes the ignition coils to remain permanently energized, literally melting the plastic coil housings in the valve cover and causing a massive engine fire hazard.",
      "Severe Coolant and Oil Mixing: While less common than the external oil leak, if the M104 head gasket fails between an oil and coolant passage, it will create a thick 'milkshake' sludge in the engine. This destroys the oil's lubricating properties and will wipe out the main bearings.",
      "Viscous Fan Explosion: If the water pump bearing collapses or the fan clutch seizes, the massive plastic cooling fan can wobble violently at high RPMs. The fan blades will impact the radiator shroud, shattering instantly and sending high-speed plastic shrapnel through the radiator core and engine bay hoses.",
      "Differential Locker Actuator Seizing: The W463 G-Class utilizes hydraulic actuators to engage the front, center, and rear differential locks. If the system is not exercised regularly or the fluid flushed, the actuators seize internally, completely disabling the vehicle's legendary off-road capabilities."
    ],
