    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. Mechanically, the all-aluminum M112 V6 block is considered one of the most reliable and maintenance-free petrol engines Mercedes-Benz ever built. True lifespan is dictated entirely by addressing oil leaks and preventing balancer pulley failure.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. It completely lacks forced induction, offering an incredibly smooth, highly linear power delivery. The absence of a turbocharger vastly simplifies the engine bay and improves reliability under harsh off-road abuse.",
