    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). The M113 utilizes an incredibly robust duplex timing chain that is practically immortal, easily outlasting the rest of the engine components. The tensioners are highly reliable, making timing chain failure virtually unheard of.",
    "injectionType": "Multi-Port Fuel Injection (MPI). Unlike modern direct injection engines, the M113 sprays fuel over the intake valves, keeping them entirely free of carbon buildup. This dramatically increases long-term reliability and heavily reduces maintenance costs.",
    "engineLifespan": "400 000 - 600 000+ km. Mechanically, the all-aluminum M113 V8 block is universally considered one of the most reliable, bulletproof, and maintenance-free petrol engines Mercedes-Benz ever built. True lifespan is dictated entirely by addressing basic oil leaks and preventing balancer pulley failure.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. It completely lacks forced induction, offering an incredibly smooth, highly linear, and massive power delivery from idle. The absence of turbochargers vastly simplifies the engine bay and guarantees absolute reliability under harsh off-road abuse.",
