    "injectionType": "Multi-Port Fuel Injection (MPI). Unlike modern direct injection engines, the M113 sprays fuel over the intake valves, keeping them entirely free of carbon buildup. This dramatically increases long-term reliability. This specific US variant utilizes a highly sensitive Evaporative Emissions (EVAP) system that frequently triggers check engine lights.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ miles. Mechanically, the all-aluminum M113 V8 block is universally considered one of the most reliable, bulletproof, and maintenance-free petrol engines Mercedes-Benz ever built. True lifespan is dictated entirely by addressing basic oil leaks and preventing balancer pulley failure.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. It completely lacks forced induction, offering an incredibly smooth, highly linear, and massive power delivery from idle. The absence of turbochargers vastly simplifies the engine bay and guarantees absolute reliability under harsh off-road abuse.",
