    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). Located at the absolute rear of the engine block against the firewall. This layout massively shortens the engine block, but if the extremely robust chains or tensioners ever fail or stretch at high mileages, it requires a financially devastating engine-out procedure.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. This extreme pressure ensures phenomenal fuel atomization, but it guarantees thick, tar-like carbon buildup on the intake valves since fuel no longer washes over them.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 350 000+ km. Mechanically, the closed-deck aluminum block and forged internals are virtually indestructible. However, the true lifespan is profoundly dictated by the extreme, relentless heat soak generated by the 'Hot-V' turbocharger layout, which slowly bakes every plastic, rubber, and electronic component in the engine bay.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo) in a 'Hot-V' configuration. Both turbochargers are mounted entirely inside the 'V' of the cylinder banks rather than on the outside. This completely eliminates turbo lag, providing instant 610 Nm of torque, but generates highly concentrated, extreme temperatures that threaten surrounding components.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.5. An incredibly complex and powerful engine management unit that tightly controls dual boost pressures and direct injection. This ECU is famously receptive to software tuning, unlocking massive, AMG-level power reserves.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "600+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, forged crankshaft, and closed-deck block are identical to the architecture used in the 500+ hp AMG models. The block handles massive boost effortlessly, with limits dictated entirely by thermal management and the transmission torque converter.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "16.5 - 19.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "11.5 - 13.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "13.5 - 15.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "22.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "9.0L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5 or MB 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is absolutely mandatory to protect the deeply buried, blazing-hot turbochargers and the highly stressed rear timing chain.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Hot-V Component Baking: The twin turbos sit inside the engine valley, generating colossal radiant heat. Over tens of thousands of kilometers, this heat slowly bakes and destroys the ignition coils, the engine wiring harness, and all surrounding plastic vacuum lines.",
      "Turbocharger Coolant Line Leaks: The thin cooling lines that supply the 'Hot-V' turbos are subjected to the most extreme thermal stress imaginable. The rubber seals inside the quick-connect fittings harden and fail, causing slow, highly damaging coolant leaks directly onto the hot engine block.",
      "Ignition Coil Failure: Because the ignition coils are mounted dangerously close to the 'Hot-V' exhaust heat, they degrade and crack much faster than on traditional engines. This leads to severe misfires under heavy boost.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves. Thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valve stems, causing random misfires and heavily restricting engine airflow. Walnut blasting is required.",
      "PCV Oil Separator Failure: The complex Positive Crankcase Ventilation system frequently fails, allowing thick oil vapors to be sucked directly into the turbochargers and intercoolers. This dramatically lowers the fuel's octane rating and heavily accelerates carbon buildup.",
      "Rear Main Seal Blowout: If the PCV system fails entirely and clogs, the resulting crankcase pressure has nowhere to safely vent. This extreme pressure will forcefully blow out the rear main seal, dumping the engine's oil supply between the engine and transmission."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Engine Overheating: If the buried turbocharger coolant lines fail significantly and dump the engine's coolant supply, the immense heat generated by the BiTurbo V8 will instantly warp the aluminum block if the driver does not immediately pull over.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Replacement Cost: Because the timing chain drive is located at the absolute rear of the engine block, access is virtually impossible while the engine is in the car. If the chain stretches, mechanics must completely remove the engine and transmission assembly, turning a standard wear item into a massive labor bill.",
      "Cylinder Scoring from Fuel Dilution: The incredibly precise direct injection system operates at massive pressures. If a piezo injector fails and becomes stuck open, raw liquid gasoline washes the lubricating oil off the NANOSLIDE cylinder walls. This lack of lubrication causes immediate, fatal scoring of the block.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The massive 610 Nm of factory torque, which dramatically increases with tuning, places immense, continuous mechanical strain on the 7G-Tronic Plus transmission clutches. If the strict 60,000-kilometer fluid service interval is bypassed, the fluid degrades rapidly, guaranteeing premature clutch pack failure.",
      "Subframe Corrosion Collapse: The rear subframe of the C238 chassis is highly susceptible to severe internal rusting, particularly in regions using heavy winter road salts. The structural metal rots entirely from the inside out, often causing the lower control arms to detach abruptly while driving at speed."
    ],
