    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. This extreme pressure ensures phenomenal fuel atomization for strict US EPA standards, but guarantees thick, tar-like carbon buildup on the intake valves over time since fuel no longer washes over them.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 250 000+ miles. Mechanically, the closed-deck aluminum block and forged internals are virtually indestructible. However, the true lifespan is profoundly dictated by the extreme, relentless heat soak generated by the 'Hot-V' turbocharger layout, which slowly bakes every plastic, rubber, and electronic component under the hood.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo) in a 'Hot-V' configuration. Both turbochargers are mounted entirely inside the 'V' of the cylinder banks rather than on the outside. This completely eliminates turbo lag and provides instant 610 Nm of torque, but generates highly concentrated, extreme temperatures that constantly threaten surrounding components.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.5. An incredibly complex and powerful engine management unit specifically calibrated for US SAE power measurements and strict OBD-II emissions monitoring. This ECU is famously receptive to software tuning, unlocking massive, AMG-level power reserves with a simple flash.",
    "euroStandard": "US EPA Tier 3",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "600+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, forged crankshaft, and closed-deck block are identical to the core architecture used in the 500+ hp AMG models. The block handles massive boost effortlessly, with limits dictated entirely by thermal management and the transmission torque converter.",
