    "injectionType": "Multi-Port Fuel Injection (MPI). Employs larger, high-flow AMG injectors spraying fuel directly over the intake valves. This keeps the valves entirely free of carbon buildup, dramatically increasing long-term reliability. This specific US variant incorporates strict EVAP and OBD-II emissions monitoring protocols.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 400 000+ miles. Mechanically, the naturally aspirated 5.4L M113 AMG block is universally considered one of the most reliable and bulletproof high-performance V8 engines ever built. True lifespan is dictated entirely by addressing peripheral oil leaks and replacing aging ignition components.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. This early US-spec G 55 AMG completely lacks forced induction. It offers an incredibly smooth, highly linear, and massive wave of torque from idle, accompanied by a signature deep, thunderous V8 exhaust note.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch Motronic ME2.8. A highly reliable, AMG-tuned engine management unit controlling the complex twin-spark ignition system. This specific version is calibrated for US SAE power measurements and strict EPA Tier 2 emissions, featuring slightly detuned throttle mapping compared to Euro models.",
