    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). The hand-built M113K AMG utilizes a massively robust duplex timing chain that is practically immortal, designed specifically to withstand the violent torque delivery of the supercharger. Timing chain failure on this specific architecture is virtually unheard of, provided basic oil maintenance is respected.",
    "injectionType": "Multi-Port Fuel Injection (MPI). Employs massively uprated, high-flow AMG injectors spraying fuel directly over the intake valves. This keeps the valves entirely free of carbon buildup, dramatically increasing long-term reliability compared to modern direct-injected AMG engines.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. Mechanically, the supercharged 5.4L M113K AMG block is universally considered one of the most reliable and bulletproof high-performance V8 engines ever built in automotive history. True lifespan is dictated entirely by addressing supercharger cooling, peripheral oil leaks, and maintaining the transmission.",
    "turboType": "IHI Lysholm Twin-Screw Supercharger. Mounted directly in the 'V' of the engine block. It provides instantaneous, devastating boost directly off idle with absolutely zero lag, accompanied by a signature, intoxicating supercharger whine.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch Motronic ME2.8.1. A highly reliable, AMG-tuned engine management unit controlling the complex twin-spark ignition system, supercharger clutch engagement, and the intercooler pump. It responds incredibly well to aftermarket software tuning and pulley upgrades.",
