    "oilSpecification": "8.5L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is highly recommended to protect the hydraulic lifters, ensure the massive V8 remains internally clean, and properly lubricate the highly stressed bearings.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Intercooler Pump Failure: The absolute most notorious flaw of the M113K. The factory Bosch intercooler pump frequently fails. When the pump dies, intake temperatures skyrocket instantly, forcing the ECU to disengage the supercharger clutch entirely. The vehicle suffers a massive, sudden loss of power.",
      "Supercharger Clutch Bearing Chirp: The electromagnetic clutch that engages the supercharger features a bearing that wears out over time. It produces a highly distinct, loud 'chirp' or squeal exactly when the supercharger engages. The bearing must be replaced to prevent catastrophic clutch failure.",
      "Harmonic Balancer (Crank Pulley) Failure: Like all M113s, the rubber vibration dampener located inside the main crankshaft pulley deteriorates. The outer ring separates and violently saws directly into the aluminum timing cover, causing massive oil leaks.",
      "Valve Cover Gasket Leaks: Due to the extreme heat generated by the massive supercharged V8, the rubber valve cover gaskets harden and leak rapidly. Oil seeps down onto the hot exhaust manifolds, causing a strong burning smell.",
      "Engine Mount Collapse: The incredibly violent 700 Nm of torque literally tears the fluid-filled engine mounts apart. A collapsed mount causes severe drivetrain vibration and can allow the engine to rock, damaging exhaust components and the supercharger belt.",
      "Twin-Spark Ignition Degradation: The M113K utilizes a complex twin-spark ignition system (two spark plugs per cylinder, 16 total). The 16 ignition wires frequently degrade from extreme heat, causing misfires that destroy the catalytic converters."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Severe Heat Soak: The supercharger generates immense heat, and the factory air-to-water intercooler system is often inadequate during repeated hard accelerations or in hot climates. The engine will rapidly pull timing to protect itself, making the 476 hp feel significantly lower until the engine cools down.",
      "Catastrophic Timing Cover Destruction: If the harmonic balancer fails and the outer ring begins to wobble, it acts like a buzzsaw against the soft aluminum timing cover. If ignored, it will cut completely through the cover, destroying the engine.",
      "Catalytic Converter Meltdown: The supercharged AMG V8 is highly sensitive to misfires caused by aging ignition coils or spark plug wires. Unburnt fuel dumps into the exhaust and instantly melts the expensive internal honeycomb of the massive catalytic converters.",
      "Rear Main Seal Oil Leaks: If the PCV system clogs with sludge, excessive internal crankcase pressure builds up. This pressure forcefully blows out the rear main seal, dumping oil between the engine and transmission.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The massive 700 Nm of supercharged torque places immense, continuous mechanical strain on the 5G-Tronic transmission. Bypassing the strict fluid service interval practically guarantees premature torque converter glazing and clutch pack failure."
    ],
