    "timingType": "Double-roller chain. The M157 utilizes an incredibly long and complex timing chain system. While late-production models (2015+) received updated secondary chain tensioners and check valves from the factory, high-mileage examples can still suffer from chain stretch. Listening for a brief metallic rattle on cold starts remains critical.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. This extreme pressure ensures phenomenal fuel atomization, but it guarantees thick, tar-like carbon buildup on the intake valves over time since fuel no longer washes over them.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000+ km. Mechanically, the engine block handles massive horsepower effortlessly, but the true lifespan is severely threatened by catastrophic cylinder wall scoring (Silitec degradation) caused by leaking fuel injectors or prolonged oil change intervals. Preventative maintenance is everything.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo). The M157 utilizes massive Garrett turbochargers mounted on the exterior exhaust manifolds. This final iteration features slightly higher factory boost mapping to achieve 571 hp, providing brutal mid-range punch and a thunderous AMG V8 roar.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.3. A highly complex and powerful engine management unit that tightly controls dual boost pressures and direct injection. This ECU is famously receptive to software tuning, unlocking massive, supercar-slaying power reserves with a simple flash.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "750+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, forged crankshaft, and robust aluminum block are heavily over-engineered. The block handles massive boost effortlessly, with tuning limits dictated strictly by the transmission torque converter limits and cooling capacity.",
