    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). The OM602 utilizes a massively over-engineered duplex timing chain that easily outlasts the vehicle itself. However, the chain is driven in conjunction with the engine vacuum pump; if the vacuum pump bearing collapses, it can drop metallic debris directly into the timing chain track.",
    "injectionType": "Indirect Injection (IDI) via pre-combustion chambers. It uses a purely mechanical Bosch PES inline injection pump. This system is entirely devoid of electronics, meaning it can run on virtually any combustible oil and is impervious to EMPs or electrical failures.",
    "engineLifespan": "500 000 - 1 000 000+ km. Mechanically, the OM602 naturally aspirated diesel is universally regarded as one of the most indestructible internal combustion engines ever created by human hands. It trades all notions of speed and refinement for absolute, post-apocalyptic longevity.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. It entirely lacks forced induction, which is the primary reason it produces only 94 horsepower. The absence of a turbocharger means extremely low internal cylinder pressures, vastly contributing to its million-kilometer lifespan.",
