    "yearRange": "1997-2001",
    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). The OM606 utilizes a massively over-engineered duplex timing chain that is practically immortal, easily capable of outlasting the engine block itself. Timing chain failure on this specific architecture is virtually unheard of.",
    "injectionType": "Indirect Injection (IDI) via pre-combustion chambers. It uses a Bosch EDC (Electronic Diesel Control) inline injection pump (often referred to as an electronically controlled mechanical pump, or ERE). This system combines the indestructible mechanical pump architecture with electronic governing for smoother operation and emissions compliance.",
    "engineLifespan": "400 000 - 800 000+ km. Mechanically, the OM606 is legendary in the automotive world, frequently referred to as the 'Diesel 2JZ' due to its immensely strong cast iron block and high-flowing 24-valve DOHC aluminum cylinder head. True lifespan is dictated by addressing fuel line air leaks and avoiding glow plug snapping.",
    "turboType": "Single Turbocharger. Utilizes a traditional, robust turbocharger equipped with a mechanical wastegate. It provides a massive leap in torque (330 Nm) over older naturally aspirated models, completely transforming the driving dynamics of the heavy G-Class.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC (Electronic Diesel Control). A rudimentary but reliable electronic management system that primarily controls the electronic governor actuator inside the Bosch inline injection pump, manages the EGR valve, and oversees the electronic glow plug relay.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 2",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "400+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, massively strong crankshaft, and thick iron block are notoriously over-engineered. The engine handles immense aftermarket turbo boost and aggressive mechanical pump upgrades (SuperTurboDiesel builds) effortlessly on completely stock internals.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "14.0 - 16.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "10.5 - 12.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "11.5 - 13.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "16.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "7.5L 5W-40 or 10W-40 Synthetic (MB 229.3 / 229.5). Strict 10,000 km oil change intervals are highly recommended to protect the turbocharger bearings and the 24 hydraulic bucket tappets.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Glow Plug Snapping: The absolute most terrifying flaw of the OM606. The long, thin glow plugs seize into the deep DOHC aluminum cylinder head due to carbon buildup. If forced during removal, they snap off flush with the head, requiring a massive labor bill or cylinder head removal to drill them out.",
      "Clear Fuel Line Air Leaks: The OM606 utilizes a complex network of clear plastic fuel lines sealed with rubber O-rings around the injection pump and fuel filter. These O-rings harden and suck air into the fuel system overnight, causing the engine to completely refuse to start until heavily cranked.",
      "EGR Valve Soot Clogging: The Exhaust Gas Recirculation (EGR) valve dumps heavy diesel soot directly into the intake manifold. Over time, this thick, tar-like sludge completely chokes the intake runners, dramatically reducing power and triggering Limp Mode.",
      "EDC Pump Actuator Wiring: The electronic actuator mounted to the back of the Bosch injection pump suffers from internal wiring insulation degradation due to engine heat, causing surging idle, stalling, and electronic pump failures.",
      "Turbo Wastegate Actuator: The vacuum-actuated wastegate controller can rust or its internal diaphragm can tear, causing a total loss of boost pressure and plunging the vehicle into a sluggish Limp Mode.",
      "Engine Mount Collapse: The immense physical weight of the inline-6 iron block crushes the fluid-filled hydraulic engine mounts over time, transmitting a harsh, brutal diesel vibration directly into the cabin at idle."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Glow Plug Extraction: If a mechanic breaks a glow plug and attempts to drill it out improperly, they will destroy the aluminum cylinder head threads, forcing a total cylinder head replacement.",
      "Air-Bound Injection System: If the clear fuel lines suck enough air, the mechanical injection pump will completely lose its prime. The owner will crank the engine until the starter motor burns out or the battery dies, completely stranding the vehicle.",
      "Transmission Conductor Plate Failure: The early 722.6 5-speed automatic transmission houses a fragile conductor plate inside the hot oil pan. Speed sensor failure will lock the transmission in 2nd gear (Limp Mode).",
      "Spring Perch Rust: While chassis-related, W463 G-Classes of this era are notorious for the rear shock and spring mounts completely rusting off the frame rails, causing the rear suspension to collapse."
    ],
    "oemPlusUpgrades": [
      {
        "name": "OM603 Mechanical Pump Conversion",
        "description": "Removing the electronically controlled EDC injection pump and retrofitting a fully mechanical Bosch PES pump from an older OM603 engine, built with larger (7mm or 8mm) elements.",
        "benefit": "The core of the 'SuperTurboDiesel' movement. This completely eliminates the restrictive ECU, allowing massive fuel delivery and turning the OM606 into a 400+ hp mechanical monster."
      },
      {
        "name": "Viton Fuel Line O-Ring Kit",
        "description": "Replacing all factory rubber O-rings in the clear fuel lines with highly durable, heat- and biodiesel-resistant Viton O-rings.",
        "benefit": "CRITICAL UPGRADE. Permanently cures the notorious OM606 air-leak issue, ensuring instant cold starts and preventing the injection pump from losing prime."
      },
      {
        "name": "EGR Delete / Intake Cleaning",
        "description": "Mechanically and electronically disabling the EGR valve, combined with a thorough chemical cleaning of the intake manifold.",
        "benefit": "Prevents thick carbon sludge from choking the engine, restoring lost horsepower and drastically improving throttle response and fuel economy."
      },
      {
        "name": "Upgraded Holset Turbocharger",
        "description": "Replacing the factory turbocharger with a larger, highly durable Holset HX35 or HX40 turbo.",
        "benefit": "Combined with a built mechanical pump, this upgrade effortlessly unlocks massive boost pressures and V8-destroying torque figures while retaining stock engine internals."
      }
    ],
