    "commonIssues": [
      "Glow plug snapping is a legendary headache for this cylinder head. The exceptionally long glow plugs tend to seize within the aluminum structure due to heavy carbon accumulation. Forcing them during extraction causes them to break flush, necessitating high removal or drilling costs.",
      "Clear fuel line air ingress remains a frequent operational issue over time. The aging plastic lines and their corresponding rubber seals dry out and flatten, allowing air to penetrate the system overnight. This results in severe hard starting conditions or complete loss of fuel prime.",
      "Delivery valve leaks on top of the fuel injection pump develop commonly as the vehicle ages. The internal O-rings and copper washers degrade under continuous thermal cycling, causing raw fuel to pool. This can lead to rough idling or erratic fuel delivery to the cylinders.",
      "EGR valve soot accumulation heavily restricts airflow through the intake manifold. Heavy diesel particulate exhaust gases mix with oil vapor, forming a thick tar-like sludge that chokes the internal ports. Sufferers will experience a noticeable drop in power and increased black smoke.",
      "Viscous fan clutch fluid degradation compromises the cooling efficiency of the massive radiator setup. Over decades, the internal silicone oil leaks out, preventing the fan from locking up under high thermal loads. This can cause rapid temperature spikes during slow off-road driving.",
      "Serpentine belt tensioner pulley shock absorber wear introduces a prominent rattling noise at idle. The small hydraulic dampener loses its internal pressure and can no longer stabilize the belt tension. Ignoring this leads to excessive belt slap and premature wear of the main accessory drive."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic cylinder head cracking occurs if the long inline-six cylinder head experiences severe overheating. Aluminum heads are highly sensitive to thermal stress, which causes metal warping and structural fractures between the valve seats. Sourcing a replacement head is an exceptionally expensive and difficult endeavor.",
      "Vacuum pump bearing failure represents an existential mechanical threat to the entire valvetrain. Early iterations of the open-bearing pump can collapse internally, dropping metal ball bearings straight into the timing chain track. This instantly snaps the duplex chain and results in terminal engine destruction.",
      "Fuel prime loss from advanced line degradation can completely immobilize the vehicle. If air ingress becomes severe, the injection pump cannot generate enough suction to pull fuel from the tank. The starter motor will often burn out before fuel pressure is successfully restored.",
      "Electronic governor actuator errors within the injection pump compromise throttle control. The internal wiring insulation bakes and crumbles, sending incorrect signals to the engine management. This can cause sudden unprompted stalling or dangerous surging while driving.",
      "Chassis spring perch corrosion is a hidden structural threat common to this era of production. The front and rear heavy-duty suspension perches can rot completely from the inside out due to road salt exposure. This causes sudden suspension collapse under heavy load or off-road stress.",
      "Differential locker actuator seizure completely deactivates the vehicle's off-road capabilities. If the hydraulic slave cylinders are not regularly flushed with fresh fluid, moisture causes the internal pistons to lock up permanently. Sourcing replacement military-grade locker components is highly expensive."
    ],
