    "oilSpecification": "8.0L 5W-30 Premium Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS MB 229.51. Strict 10,000 km intervals are absolutely critical to prevent timing chain stretch, protect the VTG turbocharger bearings, and prevent DPF ash clogging.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Oil Cooler Seal Leak: The absolute most famous and devastating flaw of the OM642. The oil cooler sits deep inside the 'V' of the engine block. The factory orange rubber seals fail due to extreme heat, leaking massive amounts of oil down the back of the engine bellhousing. Requires a massive labor bill to access.",
      "Swirl Flap Motor (M55) Contamination: The red rubber seal connecting the turbocharger intake pipe to the turbo frequently leaks oil vapor. This oil drips directly onto the electronic swirl flap actuator motor situated beneath it, short-circuiting the motor and throwing the vehicle into Limp Mode.",
      "Timing Chain Stretch: The simplex timing chain stretches over time, especially if oil changes are neglected. Causes a loud rattle on cold start. If ignored, the chain can jump teeth, destroying the valvetrain.",
      "Injector 'Black Death': The copper crush washers sealing the fuel injectors fail, allowing combustion gases and raw fuel to weep into the injector wells. This forms a thick, rock-hard black carbon crust that seizes the injectors into the cylinder head.",
      "Glow Plug Module Failure: The electronic glow plug control module frequently burns out internally, causing hard starting in cold weather and persistent check engine lights. Removing the glow plugs themselves also carries a high risk of snapping them in the cylinder head."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Limp Mode Paralysis: The OM642 is highly electronic. Any failure of the M55 swirl motor, EGR valve sticking, or DPF differential pressure sensor failure will instantly trigger Limp Mode, cutting turbo boost completely and making the heavy G-Class painfully slow.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Seizure (Black Death): If the injector blow-by leakage is ignored for thousands of kilometers, the escaping superheated combustion gases act like a cutting torch against the aluminum injector seats, destroying the cylinder head.",
      "Water Drain Blockage (SAM Module): Debris frequently blocks the cowl drains near the windshield. Water overflows directly onto the front SAM (Signal Acquisition Module), completely destroying the central electronics and immobilizing the vehicle.",
      "Conductor Plate Failure (7G-Tronic): The 722.9 automatic transmission houses its Transmission Control Module (TCM/Conductor Plate) inside the extremely hot oil pan. The delicate speed sensors on this plate frequently fail due to intense heat, throwing the transmission into Limp Mode."
    ],
