    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The OM642 engine utilizes a single-row timing chain. Due to the massive 540 Nm torque output and prolonged factory oil change intervals, the chain is notoriously prone to stretching. This causes a distinct metallic rattle on cold starts. Preventative replacement around 150,000 - 200,000 km is highly recommended to avoid catastrophic valvetrain damage.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI) utilizing highly precise Piezo injectors operating at up to 1600 bar. This generation integrates the complex SCR (Selective Catalytic Reduction) system, injecting AdBlue/DEF directly into the exhaust stream to drastically lower NOx emissions.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 450 000+ km. The fundamental aluminum block with cast-iron cylinder liners remains exceptionally robust. However, the true lifespan and daily reliability are heavily compromised by the extreme complexity and frequent failures of the BlueTEC (AdBlue) emissions control system, alongside the notorious oil cooler leaks.",
    "turboType": "Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VTG) mounted centrally inside the 'V' of the engine block. It provides excellent, lag-free low-end torque. However, its location makes it highly susceptible to heat soak and oil contamination from the adjacent PCV breather.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC17. A highly complex engine management unit that finely tunes fuel delivery, VTG operation, EGR, DPF regeneration, and the highly sensitive AdBlue (SCR) dosing system. It is notoriously strict, frequently placing the vehicle into 'countdown' Limp Mode if it detects any minor emissions anomalies.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "320+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is massively over-engineered. The identical core block handles aggressive aftermarket tuning effortlessly, with the primary limiting factors being the 7G-Tronic transmission input shaft limits and the extreme restrictiveness of the SCR/DPF exhaust system.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "14.5 - 16.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "11.0 - 13.0 L/100km",
      "mixed": "12.0 - 14.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "17.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.0L 5W-30 Premium Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS MB 229.52. Strict 10,000 km intervals are absolutely critical to prevent timing chain stretch, protect the VTG turbocharger bearings, and prevent DPF ash clogging. MB 229.52 is strictly required for SCR compatibility.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "AdBlue/SCR System Failure: The absolute defining flaw of the BlueTEC system. The NOx sensors frequently fail, the AdBlue pump dies, and the internal heater in the AdBlue tank burns out. Any of these failures trigger a terrifying 'Engine Start Not Possible in XXX km' countdown on the dashboard.",
      "Oil Cooler Seal Leak: The most famous mechanical flaw of the OM642. The oil cooler sits deep inside the 'V' of the engine block. The factory orange rubber seals fail due to extreme heat, leaking massive amounts of oil down the back of the engine bellhousing. Requires a massive labor bill to access.",
      "Swirl Flap Motor (M55) Contamination: The red rubber seal connecting the turbocharger intake pipe to the turbo frequently leaks oil vapor. This oil drips directly onto the electronic swirl flap actuator motor situated beneath it, short-circuiting the motor and throwing the vehicle into Limp Mode.",
      "Timing Chain Stretch: The simplex timing chain stretches over time, especially if oil changes are neglected. Causes a loud rattle on cold start. If ignored, the chain can jump teeth, destroying the valvetrain.",
      "Injector 'Black Death': The copper crush washers sealing the fuel injectors fail, allowing combustion gases and raw fuel to weep into the injector wells. This forms a thick, rock-hard black carbon crust that seizes the injectors into the cylinder head.",
      "Glow Plug Module Failure: The electronic glow plug control module frequently burns out internally, causing hard starting in cold weather and persistent check engine lights. Removing the glow plugs themselves also carries a high risk of snapping them in the cylinder head."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Emissions Countdown Paralysis: The BlueTEC system is unforgiving. If the NOx sensors fail or the AdBlue fluid level isn't registering properly, the ECU initiates a countdown. Once it hits zero, the vehicle is completely immobilized and will not start until expensive repairs and dealership resets are performed.",
      "Limp Mode Paralysis: The OM642 is highly electronic. Any failure of the M55 swirl motor, EGR valve sticking, or DPF differential pressure sensor failure will instantly trigger Limp Mode, cutting turbo boost completely and making the heavy G-Class painfully slow.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Seizure (Black Death): If the injector blow-by leakage is ignored for thousands of kilometers, the escaping superheated combustion gases act like a cutting torch against the aluminum injector seats, destroying the cylinder head.",
      "Water Drain Blockage (SAM Module): Debris frequently blocks the cowl drains near the windshield. Water overflows directly onto the front SAM (Signal Acquisition Module), completely destroying the central electronics and immobilizing the vehicle."
    ],
