    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the absolute rear of the engine block. The advanced inline-6 architecture places the chain drive at the transmission bellhousing side to save longitudinal space. While highly robust, any potential high-mileage stretch necessitates a devastating engine-out procedure.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 250 bar. Paired with a highly advanced 48-Volt Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) mounted directly between the engine and transmission, providing an additional EQ Boost of +20 hp and +200 Nm of instant electrical torque.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000+ km. The core aluminum block and inline-6 rotating assembly are mechanically superb and perfectly balanced. However, the true vehicle lifespan is entirely dictated by the extreme complexity and long-term viability of the 48V electrical architecture, electric auxiliary compressor, and ISG unit.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Scroll Exhaust Turbocharger + Electric Auxiliary Compressor (eZV). The 48V electric compressor spins up to 70,000 RPM in 300 milliseconds to instantly build boost off-idle, completely eliminating turbo lag until the massive conventional exhaust-driven turbocharger takes over.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. A terrifyingly complex, multi-core engine management unit coordinating the 48V mild-hybrid system, electric water pump, electric A/C compressor, exhaust turbocharger, and the electric auxiliary compressor simultaneously. Heavily encrypted.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "550+ hp. The forged internals and closed-deck block are immensely strong. However, aftermarket tuning is extraordinarily difficult due to the complex interplay between the combustion engine and the 48V EQ Boost parameters.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "12.5 - 14.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "9.5 - 11.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "10.9 - 12.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "16.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.5L 0W-20 or 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.71). Strict adherence is required to protect the ultra-precise variable valve timing, the delicate turbocharger bearings, and the sensitive OPF (Otto Particulate Filter).",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V Battery Degradation/Failure: The most catastrophic flaw of modern Mercedes MHEV platforms. The 48-Volt lithium-ion battery frequently suffers internal module or software failures. When it dies, the entire vehicle is immobilized because the 48V ISG cannot start the engine.",
      "ISG (Integrated Starter Generator) Overheating: Situated between the hot engine and transmission, the ISG can overheat under severe load. Failure requires removing the transmission to replace the electric motor, resulting in a massive labor bill.",
      "Electric Water Pump Failure: Because the M256 has NO serpentine belt, the water pump is entirely electric (48V). If it fails, the engine will overheat rapidly. There is no mechanical backup.",
      "OPF/GPF Sensor Failures: European models are equipped with an Otto Particulate Filter. The pressure differential sensors frequently fail due to soot and extreme heat, triggering Limp Mode. Short city trips will clog the ceramic matrix.",
      "Electric Auxiliary Compressor (eZV) Faults: The 48V electric turbocharger can suffer electronic board failures, causing a sudden, massive loss of low-end torque and immediate check engine lights."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Total Immobilization via 48V Failure: The M256 completely lacks a traditional 12V starter motor and a traditional serpentine belt. If the 48V system goes down, the engine cannot start, the water pump cannot flow coolant, and the A/C cannot run. You are instantly stranded.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Replacement: The rear-mounted timing chain turns a wear item into an astronomical labor expense. Mechanics must remove the engine and transmission to access the timing cover.",
      "Cylinder Scoring from Direct Injection: Operating at massive 250 bar pressures, if a piezo injector sticks open, raw fuel instantly washes the oil film off the NANOSLIDE cylinder walls, causing fatal engine block scoring.",
      "Valve Carbon Buildup: As a direct-injected engine, the intake valves never see fuel. Thick carbon sludge will accumulate heavily on the valve stems over 100,000 km, requiring professional walnut blasting."
    ],
