    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). Located at the absolute rear of the engine block against the firewall. This unconventional layout significantly shortens the overall engine block length, allowing for better weight distribution. However, if the extremely robust chains or tensioners ever fail or stretch at high mileages, it requires a financially devastating engine-out procedure.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. The US-specific AMG calibration features modified ignition timing and dumps massive amounts of fuel under load to cool the combustion chambers, ensuring compliance with EPA standards while retaining the raw AMG power.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 300 000+ miles. Mechanically, the hand-built closed-deck aluminum block and forged AMG internals are virtually indestructible. However, the true lifespan is profoundly dictated by the extreme, relentless heat soak generated by the 'Hot-V' turbocharger layout, which relentlessly bakes every plastic, rubber, and electronic component under the hood.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo) in a 'Hot-V' configuration. Both twin-scroll turbochargers are mounted entirely inside the 'V' of the cylinder banks. This completely eliminates turbo lag, providing an apocalyptic 850 Nm of torque instantaneously, but generates highly concentrated, extreme temperatures.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.5 (Dual). A highly complex engine management unit controlling the aggressive AMG dynamics, Active Cylinder Management (cylinder deactivation), and strict US EVAP emissions protocols. Because the US market lacks the restrictive OPF filter, this ECU is highly sought after for aggressive tuning.",
    "euroStandard": "US EPA Tier 3 / LEV III",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "800+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, forged AMG crankshaft, and closed-deck block are brutally strong. Without the thermal restriction of an OPF, the US-spec block handles massive aftermarket boost effortlessly, with limits dictated entirely by transmission clutch capacity.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "18.5 - 22.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "13.5 - 15.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "15.5 - 18.0 L/100km",
      "sporty": "29.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "9.0L 0W-40 or 5W-40 Fully Synthetic High-Performance (MB 229.5 or 229.51). Absolute adherence to strict 5,000-mile oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the deeply buried, blazing-hot turbochargers and the dynamic cylinder deactivation system.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Rear Main Seal (RMS) Blowout / PCV Failure: The absolute most devastating and common flaw of the M177. The Positive Crankcase Ventilation (PCV) oil separators frequently fail. This builds immense internal crankcase pressure, which violently blows out the Rear Main Seal, dumping engine oil between the block and transmission. It requires removing the transmission to fix.",
      "Hot-V Component Baking: The twin turbos sit inside the engine valley, generating colossal radiant heat. Over tens of thousands of miles, this heat slowly bakes and destroys the ignition coils, the engine wiring harness, and all surrounding plastic vacuum lines.",
      "Turbocharger Coolant Line Leaks: The thin cooling lines that supply the 'Hot-V' turbos are subjected to the most extreme thermal stress imaginable. The rubber seals inside the quick-connect fittings harden and fail over time. This causes slow, highly damaging coolant leaks directly onto the hot engine block.",
      "Ignition Coil Failure: Because the ignition coils are mounted dangerously close to the 'Hot-V' exhaust heat, they degrade and crack much faster than on traditional engines. This leads to severe misfires under heavy boost.",
      "Dynamic Engine Mount Failure: The G 63 AMG utilizes fluid-filled, electronically controlled active engine mounts to balance comfort and stiffness. The 850 Nm of torque violently tears them apart over time, leaking hydraulic fluid and causing massive chassis vibration."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Cylinder Deactivation Localized Wear: The M177 features a system that deactivates cylinders 2, 3, 5, and 8 under light load to save fuel. This can cause uneven thermal expansion and localized wear on the deactivated cylinders over high mileages. Many owners tune this feature out immediately.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Overheating: If the buried turbocharger coolant lines fail significantly and dump the engine's coolant supply rapidly, the immense heat generated by the BiTurbo V8 will instantly warp the aluminum block if the driver does not immediately pull over.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Replacement Cost: Because the timing chain drive is located at the absolute rear of the engine block, access is virtually impossible while the engine is in the car. If the chain stretches at high mileage, mechanics must completely remove the engine and transmission assembly.",
      "Cylinder Scoring from Fuel Dilution: Operating at massive 200 bar pressures, if a piezo injector fails and becomes stuck open, raw liquid gasoline washes the lubricating oil off the NANOSLIDE cylinder walls. This lack of lubrication causes immediate, fatal scoring of the engine block.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The apocalyptic 850 Nm of factory torque places immense, continuous mechanical strain on the AMG SPEEDSHIFT 9G transmission clutches. Launch control abuse or bypassing the strict fluid service interval practically guarantees premature clutch pack failure."
    ],
