    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). Located at the absolute rear of the engine block against the firewall. This unconventional layout significantly shortens the overall engine block length. However, if the extremely robust chains or tensioners ever fail or stretch at high mileages, it requires a financially devastating engine-out procedure.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. The AMG-specific calibration dumps massive amounts of fuel under load to cool the combustion chambers, ensuring survival under the immense rolling resistance of the portal axles.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 300 000+ km. Mechanically, the hand-built closed-deck aluminum block and forged AMG internals are virtually indestructible. However, the true lifespan is profoundly dictated by the extreme heat soak generated by the 'Hot-V' layout, compounded by the constant high-load demands of pushing the massive portal axle drivetrain.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo) in a 'Hot-V' configuration. Both twin-scroll turbochargers are mounted entirely inside the 'V' of the cylinder banks. This completely eliminates turbo lag, providing an apocalyptic 850 Nm of torque instantaneously, but generates highly concentrated, extreme temperatures.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.5 (Dual). The AMG variant utilizes a highly complex engine management unit controlling the aggressive AMG dynamics. Crucially for the 4x4², the ECU torque mapping is specifically calibrated to manage the immense rotational mass and protect the highly bespoke, incredibly expensive portal axle reduction gears from shearing under sudden shock loads.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6d",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "800+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, forged AMG crankshaft, and closed-deck block are brutally strong. The block handles massive aftermarket boost effortlessly, but tuning is HIGHLY discouraged due to the extreme fragility of the portal axle gearboxes under increased torque.",
