    "timingType": "Double-roller chain (Duplex). Located at the absolute rear of the engine block against the firewall. This unconventional layout significantly shortens the overall engine block length, but if the extremely robust chains or tensioners ever fail or stretch at high mileages, it requires a financially devastating engine-out procedure.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar. Paired with a highly advanced 48-Volt Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) mounted directly between the engine and transmission, providing an additional EQ Boost of +20 hp and +200 Nm of instant electrical torque.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 300 000+ km. Mechanically, the hand-built closed-deck aluminum block and forged AMG internals are virtually indestructible. However, the true lifespan is profoundly dictated by the extreme, relentless heat soak generated by the 'Hot-V' layout, compounded by the extreme complexity of the new 48V electrical architecture.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo) in a 'Hot-V' configuration. Both twin-scroll turbochargers are mounted entirely inside the 'V' of the cylinder banks. The 48V ISG completely masks any fractional turbo lag, providing an apocalyptic surge of torque instantaneously off idle.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. A terrifyingly complex, multi-core engine management unit. It must simultaneously coordinate the aggressive AMG dynamics, Active Cylinder Management (cylinder deactivation), strict Euro 6e OPF emissions protocols, and the integration of the 48V ISG mild-hybrid system. Heavily encrypted.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "800+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, forged AMG crankshaft, and closed-deck block are brutally strong. The block handles massive aftermarket boost effortlessly, with limits dictated entirely by the highly restrictive OPF filters and the fragility of the 48V ISG under modified loads.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "16.0 - 19.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "12.0 - 14.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "14.5 - 16.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "25.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "9.0L 0W-40 or 5W-40 Fully Synthetic High-Performance Low-SAPS (MB 229.51 / 229.52). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is mandatory to protect the deeply buried turbos, the cylinder deactivation system, and the OPF matrix.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V Battery Degradation/Failure: The most catastrophic flaw of modern Mercedes MHEV platforms. The 48-Volt lithium-ion battery frequently suffers internal module or software failures. When it dies, the entire vehicle is immobilized because the 48V ISG cannot start the engine.",
      "ISG (Integrated Starter Generator) Overheating: Situated tightly between the hot AMG V8 and the transmission, the ISG can overheat under severe load or launch controls. Failure requires completely removing the transmission to replace the electric motor, resulting in a massive labor bill.",
      "Rear Main Seal (RMS) Blowout / PCV Failure: The absolute most devastating and common mechanical flaw of the M177. The Positive Crankcase Ventilation (PCV) oil separators frequently fail. This builds immense internal crankcase pressure, which violently blows out the Rear Main Seal, dumping engine oil.",
      "Hot-V Component Baking: The twin turbos sit inside the engine valley, generating colossal radiant heat. Over tens of thousands of kilometers, this heat slowly bakes and destroys the ignition coils, the engine wiring harness, and all surrounding plastic vacuum lines.",
      "Turbocharger Coolant Line Leaks: The thin cooling lines that supply the 'Hot-V' turbos are subjected to the most extreme thermal stress imaginable. The rubber seals inside the quick-connect fittings harden and fail over time, causing slow, highly damaging coolant leaks.",
      "OPF/GPF Sensor Failures: European models are equipped with an Otto Particulate Filter. The pressure differential sensors frequently fail due to soot and extreme heat, triggering a Limp Mode condition. Driving strictly on short city trips will completely clog the ceramic filter matrix."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Total Immobilization via 48V Failure: The introduction of the ISG means the M177 no longer has a traditional 12V starter motor. If the highly sensitive 48V electrical architecture experiences a short circuit or voltage drop, the vehicle is instantly paralyzed and must be towed.",
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Replacement Cost: Because the timing chain drive is located at the absolute rear of the engine block, access is virtually impossible while the engine is in the car. If the chain stretches at high mileage, mechanics must completely remove the engine and transmission assembly.",
      "Cylinder Scoring from Fuel Dilution: Operating at massive 200 bar pressures, if a piezo injector fails and becomes stuck open, raw liquid gasoline washes the lubricating oil off the NANOSLIDE cylinder walls. This lack of lubrication causes immediate, fatal scoring of the engine block.",
      "OPF Thermal Runaway: The Otto Particulate Filter relies on extremely high exhaust temperatures to burn off accumulated soot. If the engine misfires due to baked ignition coils or if the sensors fail, the filter can enter a thermal runaway state, melting the internal structure.",
      "Cylinder Deactivation Localized Wear: The M177 features a system that deactivates cylinders 2, 3, 5, and 8 under light load to save fuel. This can cause uneven thermal expansion and localized wear on the deactivated cylinders over high mileages.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The apocalyptic 850 Nm of factory torque, augmented by the instant 200 Nm hit from the ISG, places immense, continuous mechanical strain on the AMG SPEEDSHIFT 9G transmission clutches. Launch control abuse guarantees premature clutch pack failure."
    ],
