    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI) utilizing advanced Piezo injectors operating at an immense 2500 bar. This generation features stepped-bowl combustion chambers and a highly complex, multi-stage SCR (Selective Catalytic Reduction) system integrated directly into the exhaust manifold to achieve near-zero NOx emissions.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 400 000+ km. Mechanically, the all-aluminum block with NANOSLIDE cylinder coating and forged steel pistons is an absolute engineering masterpiece, virtually immune to the scoring issues of older V8s. True lifespan is dictated entirely by the extreme complexity of the DPF/SCR emissions suite and rear timing chain maintenance.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo). Utilizes a smaller high-pressure turbocharger for instant off-idle response, transitioning smoothly to a massive low-pressure turbocharger for high-RPM power. Completely eliminates turbo lag while producing a massive 600 Nm of torque.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. A terrifyingly complex, multi-core engine management unit that finely tunes fuel delivery, sequential turbo transitioning, Camtronic variable valve lift, and the highly sensitive AdBlue dosing system. It is heavily encrypted to prevent aftermarket tuning and emissions defeat devices.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6d-TEMP",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "450+ hp. The internal forged steel pistons, massive crankshaft, and robust aluminum block are heavily over-engineered. The identical core engine is used in the G 400 d producing 330 hp. The block handles aggressive aftermarket tuning effortlessly.",
