    "oilSpecification": "8.5L 5W-30 Premium Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS MB 229.52. Strict 10,000 km intervals are absolutely critical to protect the sequential turbocharger bearings, the delicate NANOSLIDE cylinder walls, and prevent DPF ash clogging. MB 229.52 is strictly required for SCR compatibility.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "AdBlue/SCR System Failure: The absolute defining flaw of modern Mercedes diesels. The NOx sensors frequently fail, the AdBlue pump dies, and the internal heater in the AdBlue tank burns out. Any of these failures trigger a terrifying 'Engine Start Not Possible in XXX km' countdown on the dashboard.",
      "Camtronic Actuator Failure: The variable valve lift system relies on electronic actuators on the camshafts. If these actuators stick or fail, the engine will suffer a sudden loss of power, rough idling, and trigger Limp Mode.",
      "Complex EGR/DPF Clogging: The engine features both high-pressure and low-pressure Exhaust Gas Recirculation loops. If driven purely on short city trips, this intricate network, along with the DPF, chokes with soot rapidly, paralyzing the vehicle's electronics into Limp Mode.",
      "Coolant Pump Leaks: The highly advanced, switchable mechanical water pump can develop internal seal leaks, weeping coolant down the front of the engine block. Requires a complex replacement procedure.",
      "Rear Main Seal Oil Leaks: If the highly integrated PCV system clogs with sludge, excessive internal crankcase pressure builds up. This pressure forcefully blows out the rear main seal, dumping oil between the engine and transmission.",
      "Diesel Injector Failure: Operating at 2500 bar, the Piezo injectors are highly sensitive to fuel quality. Failure leads to uneven idling, severe 'diesel knock' under load, and potential cylinder washing."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Engine-Out Timing Chain Replacement Cost: Because the timing chain drive is located at the absolute rear of the engine block, access is virtually impossible while the engine is in the car. If the chain stretches, mechanics must completely remove the engine and transmission assembly, turning a standard wear item into a massive labor bill.",
      "Emissions Countdown Paralysis: The BlueTEC system is unforgiving. If the NOx sensors fail or the AdBlue fluid level isn't registering properly, the ECU initiates a countdown. Once it hits zero, the vehicle is completely immobilized and will not start until expensive repairs and dealership resets are performed.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Seizure (Fuel Dilution): If the immensely high-pressure (2500 bar) Piezo injectors leak, raw diesel washes the lubricating oil off the NANOSLIDE cylinder walls. This lack of lubrication causes immediate, fatal scoring of the block.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The massive torque places immense, continuous mechanical strain on the 9G-Tronic transmission clutches. Bypassing the strict fluid service interval practically guarantees premature clutch pack failure.",
      "Electrical System Voltage Drops: The second-generation W463 relies on a vastly more complex, fully digital electrical architecture compared to its predecessor. A weak battery will cause a cascade of terrifying dashboard error messages.",
      "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves. Thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valve stems, causing random misfires and heavily restricting engine airflow."
    ],
