    "yearRange": "2024-present",
    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the absolute rear of the engine block. The modernized OM656M architecture continues to place the chain drive at the transmission bellhousing side to optimize packaging constraints and crash metrics. Sufferers of high-mileage wear tracking must endure a mandatory engine-extraction labor process to access components.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI) running up to an advanced 2700 bar. Paired with a highly sophisticated 48-Volt Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) mounted directly into the transmission assembly, providing an additional temporary EQ Boost element of +20 hp and +200 Nm.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000+ km. The upgraded structural layout tracks with phenomenal power density values. However, long-term longevity metrics are bound entirely to the delicate operational health of the 48V hibrid battery arrays, complex switchable thermal routing manifolds, and highly sensitive exhaust aftertreatment electronics.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo) featuring advanced electric actuator nozzle tracking. The common rail pressures combined with immediate 48V ISG mechanical assistance eliminate low-end torque latency completely, delivering a massive 750 Nm of torque almost instantaneously from a standstill.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. Next-generation multi-processor management module executing millions of real-time calibrations to correlate high-voltage 48V hibrid recuperation cycles, Camtronic exhaust lift profiles, variable pump outputs, and strict Euro 6e multi-stage urea injection algorithms safely.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "450+ hp. The newly up-displaced block and revised steel piston profiles harbor substantial structural performance ceilings. Tuning parameters are strictly bounded by the multi-layered torque limitation handshakes shared with the 48V hibrid network and the integrated 9G-Tronic transmission clutches.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "10.0 - 11.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "7.5 - 9.0 L/100km",
      "mixed": "8.7 - 9.8 L/100km",
      "sporty": "14.5+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.5L 0W-20 or 5W-30 Premium Fully Synthetic Ultra-Low SAPS (MB 229.71 / 229.72). Rigid execution of oil maintenance limits is required to stave off early chain tracking stretch and prevent fouling the high-density particulate traps.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V Battery Module Failure: The most critical issue affecting the modern MHEV platform. The floor-mounted 48V lithium-ion battery can undergo sudden internal cell dropouts or communication faults. When a failure occurs, the entire high-voltage bus shuts down, completely disabling the ISG and leaving the vehicle dead.",
      "ISG Thermal Stacking: Sited inside the bellhousing behind the hot block, the Integrated Starter Generator is subjected to heavy thermal stress under continuous off-road use. If the internal insulation fails, a replacement requires dropping the transmission.",
      "Camtronic Valvetrain Actuator Faults: The variable exhaust lift system relies on electronic pinning sliders to toggle cam profiles. Carbon-heavy oil or actuator solenoid wear can cause the pins to stick, prompting instant check engine states and rough power curves.",
      "BlueTEC Exhaust Sensor Crashing: Meeting Euro 6e criteria demands multiple upstream and downstream NOx and particulate tracking sensors. These sensitive modules regularly undergo electrical corruption from thermal shock or soot exposure, triggering warning flags.",
      "Variable Coolant Pump Leaks: The switchable, vacuum-actuated mechanical water pump incorporates an internal slider seal to alter flow behavior. This internal diaphragm can weep fluid silently into the vacuum solenoid path, introducing a cascade of sensor errors.",
      "DPF Surcharge Loading: Despite hibrid efficiency loops, low-speed short-trip profiles cause rapid soot accumulation in the diesel particulate filter. If active regeneration cycles are consistently broken off, the filter faces structural blockage, forcing a manual workshop burn."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Total Immobilization via 48V Fault: The OM656M configuration entirely lacks a secondary, belt-driven conventional starter motor. If the 48V hibrid battery system encounters an internal short or terminal safety trip, the engine is physically incapable of starting.",
      "Astronomic Rear Chain Teardown Costs: The rear-mounted simplex timing chain configuration means that if physical wear tracks emerge at high mileages, there is no tool access. The entire engine block assembly must be split from the transmission and hoisted from the bay.",
      "Cylinder Wall Washing via Injector Over-fueling: Under extreme 2700 bar fuel delivery pressure loops, any internal structural tip defect or micro-piezo valve sticking will act like a cutting fluid jet. This washes the lubricating layer off the cylinder walls, causing terminal block scoring.",
      "SAM Module Water Flooding: The intricate digital wiring buses and signal acquisition modules sit below the primary firewall channel paths. If leaves or trail debris plug the drainage valves, rain water overflows directly into the main fuse panel, causing total electronic chaos.",
      "High-Voltage Loom Chafing Risk: The heavily shielded 48V power loops routing along the chassis frame are subjected to extreme vibration and off-road stone impacts. If the orange insulation layers break down, it presents an immediate hazard and triggers a high-voltage safety lockdown.",
      "Intake Plenum Sludge Suffocation: Direct injection architecture isolates the intake runners from fuel cleaning spray paths. Soot recirculated through the dual high/low pressure EGR networks bonds with oil mist, forming a heavy restriction layer that compromises engine respiration over time."
    ],
