    "timingType": "Double-roller chain. Early models built before late 2007/early 2008 suffered from a catastrophic metallurgical defect in the timing chain idler gear sprocket. The soft metal teeth would wear away prematurely, causing the chain to stretch and skip. Models from late 2008 onwards received a hardened, updated sprocket that permanently resolved this severe issue.",
    "injectionType": "Sequential Multi-Port Fuel Injection (MPI). The M273 beautifully utilizes traditional port injection, meaning the intake valves are constantly washed with fuel. This completely eliminates the severe carbon buildup problems that plague later direct-injected Mercedes engines.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 400 000+ km. Mechanically, the 5.5-liter all-aluminum block with Silitec cylinder linings is incredibly robust. Assuming the vehicle has the updated idler gear (or is a post-2008 model) and the intake manifold flaps are addressed, the engine easily surpasses 400,000 kilometers with routine maintenance.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. The massive 5.5L displacement relies entirely on atmospheric pressure, providing exceptionally smooth, linear power delivery and instantaneous throttle response without the immense heat soak associated with modern BiTurbo layouts.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch ME9.7. A highly reliable engine management system that precisely controls the dual-stage intake manifold and the continuously variable camshaft timing. The ECU is well-mapped but is sensitive to voltage drops from failing alternators.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 4 / Euro 5",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "450+ hp. The internal forged steel connecting rods and aluminum block are heavily over-engineered. However, since the engine is naturally aspirated, achieving significant power gains requires adding an expensive aftermarket supercharger system.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "18.5 - 22.0 L/100km",
      "highway": "12.0 - 14.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "14.0 - 16.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "24.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.5L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic MB 229.5. Strict adherence to 10,000 km oil change intervals is critical to protect the variable valve timing phasers.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Timing Chain Idler Gear Wear: The absolute most famous and devastating flaw of early M273 engines (up to early 2008). The soft metal idler sprocket wears out, triggering P0016 and P0017 camshaft timing codes. Requires massive labor to fix.",
      "Intake Manifold Tumble Flap Breakage: The plastic levers that actuate the variable intake runners become brittle from engine heat and snap. This causes the flaps to stick, resulting in poor idle, loss of low-end torque, and check engine lights.",
      "Rear Camshaft Expansion Plug Leaks: The plastic plugs sealing the rear of the camshafts shrink and leak oil directly onto the hot exhaust manifolds. This creates a burning oil smell in the cabin and requires frequent, inexpensive replacement.",
      "Camshaft Adjuster Magnet Oil Wicking: The seals inside the cam adjuster magnets fail, allowing engine oil to push through the electrical connector and travel up the wiring harness via capillary action, potentially destroying the ECU.",
      "Airmatic Suspension Collapse: While technically a chassis flaw, the extremely heavy GL 500 brutally punishes its Airmatic struts and airbags. The rubber bladders dry rot and leak overnight, causing the vehicle to sink to the ground.",
      "7G-Tronic Conductor Plate Failure: The 722.9 automatic transmission houses its control module inside the hot oil pan. The delicate turbine speed sensors frequently fail from heat exposure, locking the transmission into Limp Mode."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Engine-Out Idler Gear Replacement Cost: If you purchase a pre-2008 model that has not had the idler gear replaced, fixing the P0016 code requires removing the front engine cover or hoisting the engine out entirely, turning a parts replacement into a financially devastating labor bill.",
      "Intake Manifold Runner Ingestion: If the plastic tumble flaps disintegrate inside the intake manifold instead of just breaking at the exterior lever, the plastic fragments can be sucked directly into the combustion chamber, destroying the valves.",
      "Wiring Harness Oil Contamination: If the camshaft magnet oil wicking is ignored, the oil travels entirely through the engine harness to the oxygen sensors and the ECU. Fixing this requires replacing the entire engine wiring loom and the computer.",
      "Airmatic Compressor Burnout: If a leaking air suspension strut is ignored, the Airmatic air compressor will run continuously to keep the heavy SUV lifted. This rapidly overheats and burns out the expensive compressor motor.",
      "Front SAM Water Intrusion: The X164 chassis is notorious for clogged cowl drains. Rainwater pools up and overflows directly onto the front Signal Acquisition Module (SAM), destroying the vehicle's electrical nervous system.",
      "Valve Cover Breather Cracking: The plastic PCV breather hoses on top of the engine become incredibly brittle. They crack when handled, causing severe vacuum leaks and unmetered air entering the engine, leading to rough idling."
    ],
