    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI) utilizing Piezo injectors. This 'BlueTEC' variant incorporates the highly complex SCR (Selective Catalytic Reduction) system, injecting AdBlue/DEF directly into the exhaust stream to meet strict Euro 6 and US EPA emissions standards.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 400 000+ km. The fundamental aluminum block and cast-iron cylinder liners are robust. However, the true lifespan and daily reliability are heavily compromised by the extreme complexity and frequent failures of the early BlueTEC emissions control system, alongside the notorious OM642 oil cooler leaks.",
    "turboType": "Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VTG) mounted centrally inside the 'V' of the engine block. It provides excellent, lag-free low-end torque. However, its location makes it highly susceptible to heat soak and oil contamination from the adjacent PCV breather.",
