    "timingType": "Double-roller chain. The OM629 utilizes an incredibly complex and long timing chain system to drive all four camshafts and the high-pressure fuel pump. Despite the double-roller design, the massive 700 Nm torque output stretches the chain significantly over time. A timing chain replacement requires hoisting the massive V8 engine out of the chassis, resulting in a financially devastating labor bill.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI) via highly precise Piezo injectors operating at 1600 bar. The system utilizes two massive high-pressure fuel rails. It is highly susceptible to the infamous 'Black Death', where the copper injector crush washers fail, encasing the top of the V8 in rock-hard carbon sludge.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000 km. While the all-aluminum block itself is exceptionally strong, the engine's true lifespan is heavily compromised by chronic, cascading peripheral failures. Timing chain stretch, catastrophic fuel injector leakage, and failing twin-turbocharger vacuum networks plague the OM629. Surviving past 300k km requires an astronomical maintenance budget.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo). Utilizes two variable geometry turbochargers (VTG) mounted on the exterior exhaust manifolds. They provide incredible, lag-free torque, but the complex vacuum actuation system frequently leaks, causing sudden loss of boost and plunging the heavy vehicle into Limp Mode.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC16CP31. A complex engine management unit controlling the dual-bank architecture. It is notoriously sensitive, frequently triggering Limp Mode due to failing EGR valves, MAF sensors, or minor vacuum leaks in the twin-turbo control circuit.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 4",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "360+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and aluminum block can theoretically handle more power. However, any aftermarket tuning drastically accelerates the already catastrophic timing chain stretch and instantly overwhelms the 7G-Tronic transmission's torque limits.",
