    "timingType": "Double-roller chain. The OM629 utilizes an incredibly complex and long timing chain system to drive all four camshafts and the high-pressure fuel pump. Despite the double-roller design, the massive 700 Nm torque output stretches the chain significantly over time. A timing chain replacement requires hoisting the massive V8 engine out of the chassis, resulting in a financially devastating labor bill.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI) via highly precise Piezo injectors operating at 1600 bar. The system utilizes two massive high-pressure fuel rails. It is highly susceptible to the infamous 'Black Death', where the copper injector crush washers fail, encasing the top of the V8 in rock-hard carbon sludge.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000 km. While the all-aluminum block itself is exceptionally strong, the engine's true lifespan is heavily compromised by chronic, cascading peripheral failures. Timing chain stretch, catastrophic fuel injector leakage, and failing twin-turbocharger vacuum networks plague the OM629. Surviving past 300k km requires an astronomical maintenance budget.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo). Utilizes two variable geometry turbochargers (VTG) mounted on the exterior exhaust manifolds. They provide incredible, lag-free torque, but the complex vacuum actuation system frequently leaks, causing sudden loss of boost and plunging the heavy vehicle into Limp Mode.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC16CP31. A complex engine management unit controlling the dual-bank architecture. It is notoriously sensitive, frequently triggering Limp Mode due to failing EGR valves, MAF sensors, or minor vacuum leaks in the twin-turbo control circuit.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 4 / Euro 5 Equivalent",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "360+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods and aluminum block can theoretically handle more power. However, any aftermarket tuning drastically accelerates the already catastrophic timing chain stretch and instantly overwhelms the 7G-Tronic transmission's torque limits.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "15.0 - 17.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "10.5 - 12.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "12.0 - 14.0 L/100km",
      "sporty": "18.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "9.5L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.51). Absolute adherence to strict 10,000 km oil change intervals is the only defense against premature timing chain stretch and turbocharger bearing failure.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Catastrophic Timing Chain Stretch: The defining flaw of the OM629. The incredibly long chain stretches, causing a loud rattle on cold start. Ignoring this leads to jumped teeth and a destroyed engine. Replacement requires an engine-out procedure costing thousands of euros.",
      "Injector 'Black Death': The copper crush washers sealing the fuel injectors fail. Combustion gases and raw fuel weep into the injector wells, forming a thick, rock-hard black carbon crust that buries the injectors and erodes the aluminum cylinder head.",
      "Twin-Turbo Vacuum Leaks: The twin VTG turbochargers are controlled by a complex, fragile network of vacuum lines and transducers. These lines crack from heat, causing a total loss of boost pressure and immediate Limp Mode.",
      "Dual EGR Valve Clogging: The two Exhaust Gas Recirculation (EGR) valves dump heavy diesel soot directly into the intake manifolds. This thick, tar-like sludge completely chokes the intake runners, dramatically reducing power and triggering codes.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump Leaks: The high-pressure fuel pump frequently weeps raw diesel from its internal seals, dumping fuel down the front of the engine block and destroying the serpentine belt.",
      "Airmatic Suspension Collapse: While a chassis flaw, the extremely heavy V8 diesel brutally punishes the Airmatic struts and airbags. The rubber bladders dry rot and leak, causing the GL to sink to the ground.",
      "Water-Cooled Alternator Failure: The OM629 utilizes an incredibly expensive, liquid-cooled alternator. When it fails internally, replacing it is a massive labor ordeal requiring coolant drainage."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Engine-Out Maintenance: Because the massive BiTurbo V8 is crammed into the narrow X164 engine bay, virtually any major repair (timing chain, exhaust manifolds, turbochargers) requires removing the entire engine and transmission assembly.",
      "Transmission Torque Overload: The massive 700 Nm of torque pushes the 722.9 7G-Tronic transmission to its absolute structural limits. Torque converter shudder and conductor plate failures are extremely common.",
      "Cylinder Head Destruction: If the notorious injector 'Black Death' is ignored, the escaping superheated gases act like a cutting torch, irreparably destroying the injector seats in the aluminum cylinder heads.",
      "Limp Mode Paralysis: The OM629 is highly electronic and intensely fragile. Any failure of the MAF sensors, dual EGR valves, or vacuum transducers will instantly trigger Limp Mode, making the 2.5-ton GL painfully slow.",
      "Front SAM Water Intrusion: The X164 chassis is notorious for clogged cowl drains near the windshield. Rainwater pools up and overflows directly onto the front Signal Acquisition Module (SAM), destroying the vehicle's electrical nervous system.",
      "Airmatic Compressor Burnout: If a leaking air suspension strut is ignored, the Airmatic air compressor will run continuously to keep the heavy SUV lifted. This rapidly overheats and burns out the expensive compressor motor."
    ],
