    "timingType": "Double-roller primary chain with simplex secondary chains. The M276 BiTurbo engine is notorious for a design flaw involving the secondary timing chain tensioners. The oil bleeds out of the tensioners overnight, causing a loud, terrifying 2-3 second metallic rattle on cold starts. Installing updated tensioners and oil check valves is mandatory to prevent premature chain wear.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. This extreme pressure ensures phenomenal fuel atomization, but guarantees thick, tar-like carbon buildup on the intake valves over time since fuel no longer washes over them.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 350 000+ km. Mechanically, the 60-degree aluminum block and internal rotating assembly are extremely robust and well-balanced. True lifespan is heavily dependent on proactively fixing the timing chain tensioner issue, managing direct-injection carbon buildup, and maintaining the twin turbochargers.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo). Utilizes two compact turbochargers mounted on the exterior exhaust manifolds. They provide incredible, lag-free torque that peaks at just 1600 RPM. However, the internal wastegate actuator linkages are prone to wear, causing a rattling noise and eventual underboost conditions.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.3. A highly advanced engine management unit that finely tunes fuel delivery, variable valve timing, and twin-turbo boost curves. It is heavily favored by aftermarket tuners, as the stock 333 hp is an artificial software limitation of this highly capable engine.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "480+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is heavily over-engineered, sharing architecture with higher-output models. A simple Stage 1 ECU tune easily unlocks 400+ hp without stressing the block, making it a true hidden gem for tuning.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "12.0 - 14.0 L/100km",
      "highway": "8.5 - 10.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "9.6 - 11.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "16.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "7.0L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic MB 229.5. Strict 10,000 km intervals are absolutely critical to protect the timing chain tensioners, turbocharger bearings, and Nanoslide cylinder walls.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Cold Start Timing Chain Rattle: The defining flaw of the M276. The secondary timing chain tensioners bleed oil pressure overnight. Upon cold start, the slack chain slaps against the guides for 2-3 seconds until oil pressure builds. Requires retrofitting check valves and updated tensioners.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Wear: The mechanical HPFP driven by the camshaft degrades over time, leading to extended cranking times, lack of top-end power, and check engine lights for low rail pressure.",
      "Turbocharger Wastegate Rattle: The pivot point on the turbocharger wastegate linkage wears loose over time. This causes an annoying metallic rattle on deceleration and eventually prevents the wastegate from sealing, causing an underboost Limp Mode.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves. Thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valve stems, causing random misfires and heavily restricting engine airflow.",
      "Camshaft Adjuster Magnet Oil Wicking: The seals inside the cam adjuster magnets fail, allowing engine oil to push through the electrical connector and travel up the wiring harness via capillary action, potentially reaching the ECU.",
      "Airmatic Suspension Collapse: While technically a chassis flaw, the heavy X166 GL brutally punishes its Airmatic struts and airbags. The rubber bladders dry rot and leak overnight, causing the vehicle to sink to the ground.",
      "Ignition Coil Breakdown: The M276 utilizes a multi-spark ignition system that fires up to 4 times per millisecond. This extreme workload, combined with turbo heat, wears out the ignition coils rapidly, leading to misfires under load."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Valvetrain Destruction: If the cold-start metallic rattle of the timing chain is ignored for tens of thousands of kilometers, the chain will eventually stretch beyond the tensioner's limits, skip teeth, and cause catastrophic piston-to-valve contact.",
      "Engine Scoring from Fuel Dilution: If the high-pressure Piezo injectors stick open or leak, raw liquid gasoline washes the lubricating oil off the Nanoslide cylinder walls. This lack of lubrication causes immediate, fatal scoring of the engine block.",
      "Airmatic Compressor Burnout: If a leaking air suspension strut is ignored, the Airmatic air compressor will run continuously to keep the heavy SUV lifted. This rapidly overheats and burns out the expensive compressor motor.",
      "Catalytic Converter Meltdown: Ignoring ignition coil misfires dumps unburned fuel directly into the exhaust. The highly sensitive catalytic converters will overheat and melt internally, leading to a massive replacement bill.",
      "Wiring Harness Oil Contamination: If the camshaft magnet oil wicking is ignored, the oil travels entirely through the engine harness to the oxygen sensors and the ECU. Fixing this requires replacing the entire engine wiring loom.",
      "Front SAM Water Intrusion: The X166 chassis is notorious for clogged cowl drains. Rainwater pools up and overflows directly onto the front Signal Acquisition Module (SAM), destroying the vehicle's electrical nervous system."
    ],
