    "oilSpecification": "7.0L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic MB 229.5. Strict 10,000 km intervals are absolutely critical to protect the timing chain tensioners, turbocharger bearings, and Nanoslide cylinder walls.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Cold Start Timing Chain Rattle: The defining flaw of the M276. The secondary timing chain tensioners bleed oil pressure overnight, causing the slack chain to slap against the guides for 2-3 seconds upon cold start. Retrofitting check valves and updated tensioners is mandatory.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Wear: The mechanical HPFP driven by the camshaft degrades over time, leading to extended cranking times, lack of top-end power, and check engine lights for low rail pressure.",
      "Turbocharger Wastegate Rattle: The pivot point on the turbocharger wastegate linkage wears loose over time. This causes an annoying metallic rattle on deceleration and eventually prevents the wastegate from sealing, causing an underboost Limp Mode condition.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves. Thick, tar-like carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valve stems, causing random misfires and heavily restricting engine airflow.",
      "Camshaft Adjuster Magnet Oil Wicking: The seals inside the cam adjuster magnets fail, allowing engine oil to push through the electrical connector and travel up the wiring harness via capillary action, potentially destroying the ECU.",
      "Airmatic Suspension Collapse: While technically a chassis flaw, the heavy X166 GL brutally punishes its Airmatic struts and airbags. The rubber bladders dry rot and leak overnight, causing the vehicle to sink to the ground.",
      "Ignition Coil Breakdown: The M276 utilizes a multi-spark ignition system that fires up to 4 times per millisecond. This extreme workload, combined with turbo heat, wears out the ignition coils rapidly, leading to misfires under load."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Valvetrain Destruction: If the cold-start metallic rattle of the timing chain is ignored for tens of thousands of kilometers, the chain will eventually stretch beyond the tensioner's limits, skip teeth, and cause catastrophic piston-to-valve contact.",
      "Engine Scoring from Fuel Dilution: If the high-pressure Piezo injectors stick open or leak, raw liquid gasoline washes the lubricating oil off the NANOSLIDE cylinder walls. This lack of lubrication causes immediate, fatal scoring of the engine block.",
      "Airmatic Compressor Burnout: If a leaking air suspension strut is ignored, the Airmatic air compressor will run continuously to keep the heavy SUV lifted. This rapidly overheats and burns out the expensive compressor motor.",
      "Catalytic Converter Meltdown: Ignoring ignition coil misfires dumps unburned fuel directly into the exhaust. The highly sensitive catalytic converters will overheat and melt internally, leading to a massive replacement bill.",
      "Wiring Harness Oil Contamination: If the camshaft magnet oil wicking is ignored, the oil travels entirely through the engine harness to the oxygen sensors and the ECU. Fixing this requires replacing the entire engine wiring loom and the computer.",
      "Front SAM Water Intrusion: The X166 chassis is notorious for clogged cowl drains near the windshield. Rainwater pools up and overflows directly onto the front Signal Acquisition Module (SAM), destroying the vehicle's electrical nervous system."
    ],
    "oemPlusUpgrades": [
      {
        "name": "Timing Chain Check Valve Retrofit",
        "description": "Installing Mercedes-Benz updated secondary chain tensioners along with specialized oil check valves tapped into the cylinder heads.",
        "benefit": "CRITICAL UPGRADE. Permanently traps oil pressure in the tensioners when the engine is off, completely eliminating the terrifying cold-start death rattle and saving the timing chain."
      },
      {
        "name": "Stage 1 ECU Remap",
        "description": "Reprogramming the Bosch MED17.7.3 ECU to optimize fueling parameters and increase twin-turbo boost levels.",
        "benefit": "Safely unlocks over 430 hp and 600 Nm of torque, maximizing the potential of the factory V6 turbos and making the heavy SUV surprisingly agile without compromising reliability."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sacrificial Cam Magnet Wiring Harness Extensions",
        "description": "Installing inexpensive, factory-approved 'pigtail' harness extensions between the camshaft magnets and the main engine wiring loom.",
        "benefit": "CRITICAL UPGRADE. If the cam magnets ever leak oil internally, the oil pools in the sacrificial extension cord rather than wicking up the main harness and destroying the ECU."
      },
      {
        "name": "Inline PCV Oil Catch Can",
        "description": "Installing a high-flow inline PCV oil catch can to trap oil vapors before they enter the intake track.",
        "benefit": "Prevents oil from lowering the fuel's octane rating and drastically reduces the rate of dense carbon sludge buildup on the direct-injection intake valves."
      }
    ],
