    "timingType": "Double-roller primary chain with simplex secondary chains. The M278 V8 is notorious for a severe design flaw involving the secondary timing chain tensioners. Oil bleeds out of the tensioners overnight, causing a loud, terrifying metallic rattle on cold starts for several seconds. Installing updated tensioners and oil check valves in the cylinder heads is mandatory to prevent premature chain wear and valvetrain failure.",
