    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000+ km. Mechanically, the closed-deck aluminum block is very strong, but true lifespan is heavily dependent on two critical factors: proactively retrofitting the timing chain check valves, and perfectly maintaining the Piezo fuel injectors to prevent fatal cylinder wall scoring (Silitec degradation).",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo). Utilizes two turbochargers mounted on the exterior exhaust manifolds. They provide incredible, lag-free torque that effortlessly motivates the heavy chassis. However, the internal wastegate actuator linkages are prone to wear, causing a rattling noise and eventual underboost conditions.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.3. A highly advanced engine management unit controlling twin-turbo boost, precise Piezo fueling, and VVT parameters. It natively unlocks the full hardware potential of the M278 block compared to the artificially restricted GL 450 of the same era.",
