      "Valvetrain Destruction: If the cold-start metallic rattle of the timing chain is ignored for tens of thousands of kilometers, the chain will eventually stretch beyond the tensioner's limits, skip teeth, and cause catastrophic piston-to-valve contact.",
      "Wiring Harness Oil Contamination: If the camshaft magnet oil wicking is ignored, the oil travels entirely through the engine harness to the oxygen sensors and the ECU. Fixing this requires replacing the entire engine wiring loom and the computer.",
      "Airmatic Compressor Burnout: If a leaking air suspension strut is ignored, the Airmatic air compressor will run continuously to keep the heavy SUV lifted. This rapidly overheats and burns out the expensive compressor motor.",
      "Front SAM Water Intrusion: The X166 chassis is notorious for clogged cowl drains. Rainwater pools up and overflows directly onto the front Signal Acquisition Module (SAM), destroying the vehicle's electrical nervous system.",
      "Catalytic Converter Meltdown: Ignoring ignition coil misfires dumps unburned fuel directly into the exhaust. The highly sensitive catalytic converters will overheat and melt internally, leading to a massive replacement bill."
