    "timingType": "Double-roller primary chain with simplex secondary chains. Similar to its M278 sibling, the hand-built M157 AMG engine suffers from the notorious secondary timing chain tensioner defect. Oil bleed-down causes a severe metallic rattle on cold starts. Retrofitting the updated check valves and tensioners into the cylinder heads is a mandatory preventative measure.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at an immense 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. The AMG calibration dumps massive amounts of fuel under load to cool the combustion chambers, generating huge power but guaranteeing rapid, tar-like carbon buildup on the intake valves.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 300 000+ km. The hand-built closed-deck aluminum block and forged AMG internals are virtually indestructible under load. However, lifespan is brutally dictated by preventing cylinder wall scoring (from leaking Piezo injectors) and addressing the timing chain tensioner rattle before chain stretch occurs.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Turbochargers (BiTurbo). Massive AMG-specific twin-scroll turbochargers mounted on the exterior exhaust manifolds. The Performance Package increases factory maximum boost pressure from 1.0 bar to 1.3 bar, providing a terrifying 800 Nm of torque instantaneously. Generates extreme under-hood temperatures.",
