    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The M270 engine family is notorious for premature wear on the Variable Valve Timing (VVT) camshaft adjusters (phasers). This wear causes the internal locking pin to fail, resulting in a loud metallic rattle on cold starts for 2-3 seconds. If ignored, it accelerates timing chain stretch and guide wear.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar. This high-pressure system atomizes fuel perfectly for efficiency but completely bypasses the intake valves. This guarantees thick, tar-like carbon buildup on the intake valve stems over high mileages, requiring physical walnut blasting.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000+ km. The core aluminum block is structurally robust. However, the engine's lifespan is heavily dependent on addressing the inevitable VVT camshaft adjuster failure early, keeping the intake valves clean from carbon, and strictly maintaining the 7G-DCT transmission.",
    "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger (IHI). Very compact and highly responsive, providing maximum 250 Nm torque at just 1,250 RPM. The internal wastegate pivot can wear over time, causing a rattling noise on deceleration and eventual underboost Limp Mode codes.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.2. A highly sophisticated engine management unit. For specific markets like Russia and certain parts of Asia, this ECU features a software detune capping output at exactly 150 hp to comply with strict luxury/horsepower tax brackets, despite having the exact same hardware as the 156 hp European model.",
