    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The 2.0L M270 engine family is notorious for premature wear on the Variable Valve Timing (VVT) camshaft adjusters (phasers). This wear causes the internal locking pin to fail, resulting in a loud metallic rattle on cold starts for 2-3 seconds. If ignored, it accelerates timing chain stretch and guide wear.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. This extreme pressure ensures phenomenal fuel atomization, but guarantees thick, tar-like carbon buildup on the intake valve stems over time since fuel no longer washes over them.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000+ km. The core 2.0L aluminum block is structurally robust. However, the engine's lifespan is heavily dependent on addressing the inevitable VVT camshaft adjuster failure early, keeping the intake valves clean from carbon, and strictly maintaining the 7G-DCT transmission and the 4MATIC PTU.",
    "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger (IHI). Very compact and highly responsive, providing maximum 300 Nm torque at just 1,200 RPM. The internal wastegate pivot can wear over time, causing a rattling noise on deceleration and eventual underboost codes.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.2. A highly sophisticated engine management unit. For this specific 184 hp GLA 220, the ECU contains a strict artificial software restriction. The engine hardware is 100% identical to the 211 hp GLA 250, making it an incredibly lucrative candidate for aftermarket tuning.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6 / ULEV",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "300+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is heavily over-engineered. The block handles aggressive tuning effortlessly, with the primary limiting factors being the physical airflow limits of the stock turbocharger and the dual-clutch transmission's torque capacity.",
