    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. Like the standard M270, this Flex-Fuel engine is notorious for premature wear on the Variable Valve Timing (VVT) camshaft adjusters. This wear causes the internal locking pin to fail, resulting in a loud metallic rattle on cold starts for 2-3 seconds. If ignored, it accelerates timing chain stretch.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar. This Brazil-market specific model utilizes upgraded fuel lines, specialized injector seals, and software parameters to handle highly corrosive E100 (100% Ethanol) fuel without degrading the fuel system components.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 300 000+ km. Lifespan is highly dependent on oil maintenance. Because ethanol requires significantly more fuel volume to achieve stoich, and burns cooler, unburned ethanol frequently washes past the piston rings on cold starts, diluting the engine oil much faster than standard petrol models.",
    "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger (IHI). Very compact and highly responsive, providing maximum 350 Nm torque. The internal wastegate pivot can wear over time, causing a rattling noise on deceleration.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.2 (Flex). A highly sophisticated engine management unit featuring specific flex-fuel mapping. It constantly reads fuel composition sensors to adjust ignition timing and fuel volume dynamically based on the current ethanol blend in the tank.",
    "euroStandard": "Local Brazil Emissions Standard",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "320+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is identical to the standard GLA 250. However, because E100 ethanol has an incredibly high octane rating (~105+ AKI) and massive cooling properties, this engine can be tuned much more aggressively on E100 than the standard petrol version without knocking.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "11.0 - 13.0 L/100km (E100)",
      "highway": "8.0 - 9.5 L/100km (E100)",
      "mixed": "9.5 - 11.5 L/100km (E100)",
      "sporty": "14.5+ L/100km (E100)"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "5.8L 5W-40 Fully Synthetic MB 229.5. CRITICAL: For Flex-Fuel models running high ethanol content, oil change intervals MUST be shortened to 7,000 km to prevent severe oil dilution and premature timing chain wear.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Severe Oil Dilution: Ethanol burns cooler and requires more volume. On cold starts, unburned ethanol blows past the piston rings and dilutes the engine oil, destroying its lubricating properties and accelerating timing chain and bearing wear.",
      "Camshaft Adjuster (VVT Phaser) Rattle: The absolute defining flaw of the M270. The internal locking mechanism in the camshaft adjusters wears out. This causes a terrifying metallic clatter on cold starts.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Overwork: Because E100 requires roughly 30% more fuel volume than petrol, the mechanical HPFP works significantly harder, leading to premature wear, long cranks, and low rail pressure codes.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves. Thick carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the valve stems, causing rough idling and heavily restricting engine airflow.",
      "Thermostat Failure: The electronically mapped thermostat frequently sticks open, preventing the engine from reaching optimal operating temperature.",
      "Coolant Pump Leaks: The water pump features a plastic housing that warps from heat cycling, causing coolant to weep down the front of the engine block.",
      "7G-DCT Dual Clutch Judder: The 7-speed dual-clutch transmission can suffer from rough shifts and low-speed juddering if the fluid is degraded."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Valvetrain Destruction via Diluted Oil: If oil is not changed frequently while running E100, the thinned, ethanol-diluted oil fails to protect the timing chain and VVT adjusters, rapidly accelerating chain stretch and causing catastrophic piston-to-valve contact.",
      "Intake Valve Seat Burning: If severe carbon buildup on the intake valves is ignored, the valves may fail to seat and seal properly. Hot combustion gases will escape past the valves, burning the edges and requiring a cylinder head rebuild.",
      "Engine Overheating via Plastic Pump Failure: A sudden structural failure of the plastic water pump housing can rapidly dump the engine's coolant supply. If the driver does not notice the temperature gauge, the aluminum block will warp.",
      "Mechatronic Unit Failure (7G-DCT): Skipping the mandatory transmission fluid changes leads to metallic debris circulating through the delicate solenoids of the 7G-DCT mechatronic unit, eventually requiring a highly expensive replacement.",
      "Turbocharger Wastegate Wear: The pivot point on the turbocharger wastegate linkage wears loose. This not only causes an annoying rattle but eventually prevents the wastegate from sealing, causing an underboost Limp Mode.",
      "PTU Destruction (4MATIC): If the whining noise from a failing Power Transfer Unit bearing is ignored, the unit can catastrophically seize, severely damaging the attached 7G-DCT transmission housing."
    ],
