    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The hand-built M133 AMG engine features significantly reinforced timing components to handle the violent RPM climbing and massive boost pressures. Timing chain stretch is rare if the strict oil intervals are respected, though the chain tensioner should be monitored past 150,000 km.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 bar via highly precise Piezo injectors. The system relies on a heavily uprated High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) to feed the extreme fuel demands of 1.9 bar of boost (increased for the facelift). Carbon buildup on the intake valves is a guaranteed issue over time.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 250 000+ km. The engine block is astonishingly strong, utilizing a sand-cast closed-deck design and fully forged internals. The facelift model features refined valve timing and software, but peripheral components like the turbocharger, PCV system, and ignition coils remain pushed to their absolute thermal limits.",
    "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger (BorgWarner). A massive, heavily reinforced unit operating at a terrifying 1.9 bar (27.5 psi) of stock boost in the facelift model. It generates immense heat. The wastegate pivot and actuator rod are known to wear out, causing a metallic rattle on deceleration and loss of peak boost.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.2. A highly customized AMG engine management unit. The facelift model features heavily revised software, altered exhaust valve timing, and higher peak boost to achieve 381 hp. It orchestrates complex multi-spark ignition and aggressive exhaust flap control.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "450+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, forged pistons, and sand-cast block are virtually indestructible under Stage 1 or Stage 2 tuning. The absolute limiting factors are the thermal capacity of the intercooler and the clamping force of the 7-speed DCT transmission clutches.",
