      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: The defining mechanical nightmare of the OM651. The single-row chain stretches, causing a loud rattle on cold start. Ignoring this leads to jumped teeth and destroyed valves. Replacement requires engine/transmission removal.",
      "Water Pump Leak: The OM651 uses a complex water pump with a vacuum-actuated shroud to heat the engine faster. The plastic housing warps and leaks coolant heavily down the front of the block.",
      "Intake Manifold Flap Actuator Failure: The plastic linkages connecting the intake manifold swirl flaps snap. This causes the flaps to stick, resulting in Limp Mode and a severe loss of low-end torque.",
