    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. The OM651 is infamous for timing chain stretch. Because the chain is located against the firewall, replacing it requires removing the transmission or hoisting the entire engine out of the vehicle, resulting in a terrifying labor bill. A metallic rattle on cold starts is the early warning sign.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI). Operates via magnetic solenoid injectors. The facelift Euro 6 variants feature refined injection mapping, but injector copper seal failure ('Black Death') remains a highly common issue.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. The cast-iron block itself is virtually indestructible. The engine's true lifespan is entirely dictated by addressing the rear-mounted timing chain stretch, replacing the plastic water pump, and dealing with the increased complexity of the Euro 6 exhaust aftertreatment system.",
    "turboType": "Single Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VTG). Highly responsive. The facelift model features slight tweaks to improve efficiency and reduce turbo lag, but remains prone to heat soak and DPF backpressure issues if driven exclusively in the city.",
