      "commonIssues": [
        "Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) Clogging: Vehicles driven exclusively on short, low-speed city trips fail to reach the exhaust temperatures required for GPF regeneration, causing the filter to choke and triggering Limp Mode.",
        "Electronic Thermostat Housing / Water Pump Leaks: The M282 uses a complex thermal management module. The plastic housing is prone to warping from heat cycling, leading to slow coolant leaks.",
        "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Because fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes over the intake valves. Carbon sludge builds up on the valve stems over 80,000 km, causing rough idling.",
        "Electronic Wastegate Actuator Sticking: The electronic arm controlling the turbo wastegate can seize due to intense heat from the integrated exhaust manifold, causing underboost or overboost codes.",
        "7G-DCT Dual Clutch Judder: The 7-speed dual-clutch transmission can suffer from low-speed juddering or harsh downshifts if the transmission fluid changes are neglected.",
        "Spark Plug Wear: The advanced combustion strategies (and cylinder deactivation) are extremely sensitive to spark plug gap. Plugs must be changed strictly on schedule to prevent misfires.",
        "Oil Dilution: Direct injection engines running rich on cold starts can allow fuel to blow past the rings into the oil pan, especially on vehicles that never reach full operating temperature."
      ],
      "vulnerabilities": [
        "GPF Destruction: Ignoring GPF warning lights and continuing to drive short trips will permanently clog the filter, requiring an astronomically expensive replacement.",
        "Engine Overheating: A sudden structural failure or severe warp of the plastic thermal management module can dump the engine's coolant supply, warping the aluminum 'Delta' cylinder head.",
        "Mechatronic Unit Failure (7G-DCT): Skipping the mandatory transmission fluid changes leads to metallic debris circulating through the delicate solenoids of the 7G-DCT, eventually requiring replacement.",
        "Intake Valve Seat Burning: If severe carbon buildup on the intake valves is ignored, the valves may fail to seat properly. Hot combustion gases will escape past the valves, burning the edges.",
        "Premature Bearing Wear via Oil Dilution: If fuel dilutes the engine oil and the oil is not changed frequently (e.g., following the absurd 25,000 km factory interval), the connecting rod bearings will suffer accelerated wear."
      ],
