    "oilSpecification": "5.1L 0W-20 Fully Synthetic Low-Ash (MB 229.71). CRITICAL: Must use low-ash oil to prevent the Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) from clogging permanently.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "48V RSG Belt Wear: The Belt-Driven Starter-Generator places immense torque loads on the serpentine belt to start the engine and provide EQ Boost. Belt squeal or premature wear is common and requires strict replacement intervals.",
      "48V System Software Glitches: Early MHEV models can suffer from software anomalies where the 48V battery fails to charge or the EQ Boost cuts out, triggering an array of dashboard warnings.",
      "Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) Clogging: Vehicles driven exclusively on short, low-speed city trips fail to reach the exhaust temperatures required for GPF regeneration, causing the filter to choke and triggering Limp Mode.",
      "Electronic Thermostat Housing Leaks: The M282 uses a complex thermal management module. The plastic housing is prone to warping from heat cycling, leading to slow coolant leaks.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Thick carbon sludge builds up on the intake valve stems over 80,000 km, causing rough idling and disrupting the cylinder deactivation system.",
      "Spark Plug Sensitivity: The cylinder deactivation system is extremely sensitive to spark plug gap. Plugs must be changed strictly on schedule to prevent misfires on cylinders 2 and 3."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "48V Battery Degradation: The lithium-ion 48V battery is a highly expensive component. If the vehicle is parked for extended periods without a trickle charger, the battery can degrade completely, immobilizing the vehicle.",
      "GPF Destruction: Ignoring GPF warning lights and continuing to drive short trips will permanently clog the filter, requiring an astronomically expensive replacement.",
      "Engine Overheating: A sudden structural failure or severe warp of the plastic thermal management module can dump the engine's coolant supply, warping the aluminum cylinder head.",
      "Mechatronic Unit Failure (7G-DCT): Skipping the mandatory transmission fluid changes leads to metallic debris circulating through the delicate solenoids of the 7G-DCT, eventually requiring replacement.",
      "Belt Snap Engine Damage: If the heavily stressed 48V RSG serpentine belt snaps, it can potentially wrap around the crankshaft pulley and damage the front main seal."
    ],
