    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 350 bar (increased from 250 bar on older models). Integrated with a 48V Integrated Starter-Generator (ISG). Unlike the RSG, the ISG sits directly between the engine and transmission, eliminating the serpentine belt entirely. Direct injection inherently guarantees intake valve carbon buildup over high mileages.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 350 000+ km. The core aluminum block (NANOSLIDE, CONICSHAPE) is a masterclass in modern engineering, completely solving the notorious cylinder head issues of the older M260. However, true lifespan is heavily dependent on the longevity of the highly complex 48V electrical architecture, the ISG unit, and GPF maintenance.",
    "turboType": "Advanced Twin-Scroll Turbocharger with an overboost function developed with Mercedes-AMG F1 technology. It provides incredibly fast spooling. The 48V ISG EQ Boost system completely masks any remaining low-RPM turbo lag, providing instant electric torque.",
