    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The M260 engine features a significantly reinforced timing chain and Variable Valve Timing (VVT) architecture compared to the older M270. In the AMG 35 models, these components handle the aggressive RPM climbing excellently, provided the oil is changed strictly on time.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 250 bar via centrally positioned piezo injectors. Equipped with a Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF/OPF) to comply with Euro 6d emissions. Direct injection combined with AMG boost levels guarantees intake valve carbon buildup over time.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 250 000+ km. The core aluminum block featuring CONICSHAPE cylinder honing and NANOSLIDE coating is incredibly durable. However, the M260 engine (even in AMG guise) has a notorious, highly documented flaw regarding premature exhaust valve seat wear in the cylinder head, which can drastically cut the engine's lifespan short.",
    "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger. The AMG variant utilizes a larger, specifically tuned twin-scroll exhaust gas turbocharger with an electronically controlled wastegate. It provides exceptional throttle response and holds 400 Nm of torque across a broad rev range.",
