      "Catastrophic Cylinder Head Failure: If misfires (caused by exhaust valve seat warping) are ignored, the engine will lose compression completely, requiring an astronomically expensive repair.",
      "GPF Destruction: Ignoring GPF warning lights and continuing to drive short trips will permanently clog the filter, requiring a highly expensive replacement.",
      "Engine Overheating: A sudden structural failure of the plastic thermal management module can dump the engine's coolant supply, warping the aluminum block.",
      "Mechatronic Unit Failure (8G-DCT): Skipping mandatory transmission fluid changes leads to metallic debris circulating through the delicate solenoids.",
