    "oilSpecification": "5.5L 0W-20 or 5W-30 Fully Synthetic High-Performance Low-Ash (MB 229.71). CRITICAL: Due to the extreme 1.9 bar boost and the sensitive roller-bearing turbocharger, oil MUST be changed strictly every 8,000 km.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Turbocharger Heat Soak: Because the M139 is rotated 180 degrees, the massive turbocharger is jammed directly against the firewall. Despite extensive heat shielding, this radiant heat frequently degrades surrounding plastic components and sensors.",
      "AMG 8G-DCT Judder & Clunking: The heavily reinforced 8-speed DCT can be brutal and clunky in low-speed, stop-and-go traffic. Launch control abuse significantly accelerates clutch wear and degradation of the hydraulic fluid.",
      "4MATIC+ Rear Differential Wear: The rear differential features two electronically controlled multi-disc clutches (AMG Torque Control). If driven aggressively without religious fluid changes, these clutch packs wear out prematurely, causing binding and whining.",
      "Spark Plug Degradation: The intense cylinder pressures and multi-spark ignition system obliterate spark plugs. They must be replaced exactly on schedule, or the resulting misfires will immediately trigger Limp Mode to protect the engine.",
      "Electric Water Pump Failures: The engine utilizes multiple electric water pumps to cool the block, turbo, and intercooler after shut-off. If one fails, the vehicle will severely overheat the charge air, dropping boost entirely.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Strain: The mechanical HPFP works incredibly hard to supply the direct injectors under peak boost. Early degradation leads to long crank times and sudden power cuts at high RPMs.",
      "Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) Choking: Driven exclusively in the city, the exhaust will not reach the temperatures required to burn off soot, forcing the GPF to clog and drastically cutting power."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Rear Differential Seizure: If the twin multi-disc clutches in the AMG Torque Control rear axle are starved of clean fluid, they will fuse together or seize, requiring a total differential replacement costing thousands of euros.",
      "Turbocharger Bearing Failure: The roller bearings in the turbo are highly sensitive to oil quality. Stretched oil change intervals will introduce micro-abrasives that instantly destroy the expensive twin-scroll turbocharger.",
      "Transmission Mechatronic Destruction: Metallic debris from the aggressive AMG clutch packs will circulate through the 8G-DCT's valve body if the fluid isn't changed perfectly on schedule, destroying the solenoids.",
      "Firewall & Harness Melting: If the specialized turbo heat shields are damaged or removed by careless mechanics, the intense exhaust temperatures will literally melt the engine wiring harness and plastic cowl components.",
      "Piston Ring Land Cracking: Using low-octane fuel under high boost conditions will cause severe engine knock. Despite being forged, repeated knock will shatter the piston ring lands.",
      "GPF Destruction: Ignoring GPF regeneration warnings will permanently solidify the soot in the filter, requiring an astronomically expensive exhaust replacement."
    ],
