    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The M139 is a completely bespoke engine designed from scratch by AMG. It features a heavily reinforced timing chain system optimized for extreme 7,200 RPM operation. Timing chain stretch is virtually nonexistent if the strict 8,000 km oil intervals are followed.",
    "injectionType": "Dual-Stage Injection System. Operates via both Direct Injection (CGI) at up to 200 bar and secondary Port Fuel Injection (PFI). This ingenious setup not only fuels the massive 2.1 bar boost requirements but also washes the intake valves with fuel, completely eliminating the carbon buildup issues that plagued older engines.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 250 000+ km. The sand-cast, closed-deck aluminum block with NANOSLIDE coating and forged internals is built like a race engine. However, lifespan is brutally dictated by thermal management. The engine is rotated 180 degrees (turbo at the firewall), subjecting the rear of the engine bay to apocalyptic temperatures.",
    "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Roller-Bearing Turbocharger. Pushing a staggering 2.1 bar (30.5 psi) in the 'S' model, making it the most powerful production 4-cylinder turbo in the world. The roller bearings allow it to spool remarkably fast for its massive size. It is cooled by oil, water, and fresh air ducted from the front grille.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.7. An absolute supercomputer of an ECU, managing the complex dual-stage injection, dual electronic water pumps, extremely precise wastegate control, and the AMG Torque Control rear differential.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6d / Euro 6d-ISC-FCM",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "500+ hp. The internal forged connecting rods, forged pistons, and sand-cast block are indestructible at these levels. The limiting factors are the thermal capacity of the intercooler, the turbocharger's physical airflow limit, and the clamping force of the 8G-DCT transmission.",
