    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The M282 represents a massive reliability upgrade over older generations. It utilizes a highly robust timing chain layout. Premature stretch or VVT failure is exceptionally rare as long as strict low-ash oil change intervals are adhered to.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 250 bar via central 6-hole injectors. Integrated with a 48V Belt-Driven Starter-Generator (RSG) system. This setup provides seamless start-stop operation and EQ Boost, but direct injection inherently guarantees intake valve carbon buildup over high mileages.",
    "engineLifespan": "180 000 - 280 000+ km. The core aluminum block (co-developed with Renault/Nissan) is incredibly durable. However, the true lifespan is heavily dependent on the longevity of the 48V electrical architecture, GPF maintenance, and acknowledging that the heavy GLB chassis puts immense strain on this small displacement engine.",
    "turboType": "Single Mono-Scroll Turbocharger with an electronic wastegate actuator. Tightly integrated into the 'Delta' cylinder head. The 48V EQ Boost system provides instant electric torque off the line, masking the turbo lag and helping to get the heavy GLB chassis moving from a dead stop.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17. A highly advanced engine management system controlling the 48V hybrid integration, cylinder deactivation (ACT), and GPF regeneration. In the GLB 180, this ECU artificially restricts the 1.33L hardware, which shares its mechanicals with the more powerful GLB 200.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "200+ hp. The internal rotating assembly handles tuning effortlessly. However, tuning mild-hybrid variants is highly complex due to the 48V integration and the thermal limitations of pulling a heavy 7-seater SUV.",
