    "engineLifespan": "180 000 - 280 000+ km. The core aluminum block (co-developed with Renault/Nissan) is incredibly durable. However, the true lifespan is heavily dependent on the longevity of the 48V electrical architecture, GPF maintenance, and acknowledging that the heavy GLB chassis puts immense strain on this small displacement engine.",
    "turboType": "Single Mono-Scroll Turbocharger with an electronic wastegate actuator. Tightly integrated into the 'Delta' cylinder head. The 48V EQ Boost system provides instant electric torque off the line, masking the turbo lag and helping to get the heavy GLB chassis moving from a dead stop.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17. A highly advanced engine management system controlling the 48V hybrid integration, cylinder deactivation (ACT), and GPF regeneration. This facelift variant sees base torque increased to 270 Nm, completely optimizing the 1.33L hardware for Euro 6e.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e",
