    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The M260 engine features a significantly reinforced timing chain and Variable Valve Timing (VVT) architecture compared to the older M270 generation. Premature stretch is exceptionally rare as long as strict low-ash oil change intervals are adhered to.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 250 bar via centrally positioned piezo injectors. Integrated with a 48V Belt-Driven Starter-Generator (RSG) system. This setup provides seamless start-stop operation and EQ Boost, but direct injection inherently guarantees intake valve carbon buildup over high mileages.",
    "engineLifespan": "180 000 - 280 000+ km. The core aluminum block featuring CONICSHAPE cylinder honing and NANOSLIDE coating is incredibly durable. The facelift versions usually feature the factory-revised cylinder head, mitigating the catastrophic older valve seat failure. However, the true lifespan in the heavy GLB chassis is heavily dependent on the longevity of the 48V electrical architecture and GPF maintenance.",
    "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger with an electronically controlled wastegate. The 48V EQ Boost system provides instant electric torque off the line, completely masking any initial turbo lag and helping to effortlessly get the heavy 7-seater GLB chassis moving from a dead stop.",
