    "oilSpecification": "5.5L 0W-20 or 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-Ash (MB 229.71 or MB 229.52). CRITICAL: Must use low-ash oil to prevent the GPF from clogging. AMG models require strictly shortened intervals (8,000 km).",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Cylinder Head Valve Seat Failure: The most devastating flaw of the M260. The exhaust valve seats degrade and warp prematurely under high heat. This causes a loss of compression, resulting in rough idling, check engine lights (P0300), and requires a completely new revised cylinder head.",
      "Gasoline Particulate Filter (GPF) Clogging: The AMG 35 produces massive amounts of exhaust heat, but if driven exclusively on short city trips, it fails to reach the sustained temperatures required for GPF regeneration, causing the filter to choke.",
      "Electronic Thermostat Housing Leaks: The plastic thermal management housing is prone to warping from heat cycling under the intense thermal load of the AMG tuning and heavy chassis, leading to slow coolant leaks.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Thick carbon sludge builds up rapidly on the intake valve stems over 60,000 km due to high boost blow-by.",
      "AMG 8G-DCT Shifting Issues: The 8-speed AMG SPEEDSHIFT dual-clutch transmission can suffer from low-speed juddering or clunking if fluid changes are neglected or if subjected to excessive Launch Control abuse.",
      "Electronic Wastegate Actuator Sticking: The electronic arm controlling the AMG turbo wastegate can seize due to intense radiant heat from the integrated exhaust manifold.",
      "4MATIC PTU Bearing Wear: The Power Transfer Unit (PTU) integrated into the transmission runs extremely hot pulling the GLB's weight. Neglecting its tiny fluid capacity leads to bearing whine and failure."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Cylinder Head Failure: If the early signs of misfires (caused by the exhaust valve seats warping) are ignored, the engine will lose compression completely on the affected cylinders, requiring an astronomically expensive cylinder head replacement.",
      "PTU Destruction (4MATIC): If the whining noise from a failing Power Transfer Unit bearing is ignored, the unit can catastrophically seize, severely damaging the attached 8G-DCT transmission housing.",
      "GPF Destruction: Ignoring GPF warning lights and continuing to drive short trips will permanently clog the filter, requiring a highly expensive replacement.",
      "Mechatronic Unit Failure (8G-DCT): Skipping the mandatory transmission fluid changes leads to metallic debris circulating through the delicate solenoids of the 8G-DCT, eventually requiring replacement.",
      "Engine Overheating: A sudden structural failure of the plastic thermal management module can dump the engine's coolant supply, warping the aluminum block.",
      "Intake Valve Seat Burning: Severe carbon buildup on the intake valves can prevent proper sealing, allowing hot combustion gases to escape and burn the valve edges."
    ],
