    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. The M260 engine features a significantly reinforced timing chain and Variable Valve Timing (VVT) architecture. In the heavy, facelifted AMG 35 models, these components handle the aggressive RPM climbing excellently, provided the low-ash oil is changed strictly on time.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 250 bar via centrally positioned piezo injectors. This facelift model integrates a 48V Belt-Driven Starter-Generator (RSG) system. This setup provides seamless start-stop operation and EQ Boost, but direct injection inherently guarantees intake valve carbon buildup.",
    "engineLifespan": "150 000 - 250 000+ km. The core aluminum block (CONICSHAPE) is incredibly durable. The facelift versions usually come with the factory-revised cylinder head, mitigating the older valve seat failure. However, true lifespan is heavily dependent on the longevity of the 48V electrical architecture, GPF maintenance, and the constant thermal stress of pulling a heavy SUV.",
    "turboType": "Single Twin-Scroll Turbocharger. The AMG variant utilizes a larger, specifically tuned twin-scroll exhaust gas turbocharger. The 48V EQ Boost system completely masks any low-RPM turbo lag, providing instant electric torque off the line to get the heavy GLB moving.",
