    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. While the OM654 chain architecture is far more robust than the older OM651, it is still mounted against the firewall. If premature stretch occurs due to extended oil intervals under the heavy load of the GLB chassis, replacing the chain requires an enormously expensive engine or transmission-out service.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI). Features a highly advanced Bosch injection system operating at an extreme 2500 Bar. This unrestricted hardware allows for phenomenal fuel atomization and massive torque delivery, but the piezo-solenoid injectors are highly sensitive to fuel quality.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 500 000+ km. The OM654 is an engineering masterpiece featuring an aluminum block with steel stepped-bowl pistons and NANOSLIDE coating. The block itself is virtually indestructible. Lifespan is dictated entirely by maintaining the complex twin-SCR emissions system and proactively preventing coolant-vacuum leaks.",
