    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) via high-pressure piezo injectors. As with most direct-injected engines, it is susceptible to carbon sludge buildup on the intake valves over higher mileages.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000+ km. Lifespan is highly dependent on strict 10,000 km oil changes to protect the VVT adjusters and turbocharger. If the camshaft adjusters are proactively maintained, the block is highly durable.",
    "turboType": "Single IHI Turbocharger with an electronic wastegate. Spools very quickly, providing peak torque from just 1,200 RPM, which makes the 4MATIC-equipped GLK feel very agile in traffic.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.2. A highly sophisticated engine management system controlling boost and direct injection. In the GLK 250, this hardware runs a more aggressive, open factory map compared to the restricted GLK 200.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "260+ hp. The internal rotating assembly handles Stage 1 tuning well. However, early M274 engines have a known sensitivity in the piston wrist-pins, so extreme boost pressures should be avoided.",
