    "timingType": "Duplex timing chain. The infamous M272 balance shaft gear metallurgical defect (which annihilated engines from 2005-2007) was fully resolved by the time the GLK launched. The chain system in this 3.5L block is highly robust, provided the immense 8-liter oil capacity is refreshed religiously.",
    "injectionType": "Multi-Point Port Fuel Injection (MPI). Uses highly reliable Bosch solenoid injectors spraying directly over the intake valves. This old-school architecture inherently washes the valves with fuel, completely preventing the catastrophic carbon sludge buildup seen in modern direct-injected engines.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 450 000+ km. A practically bulletproof naturally aspirated block. If you fix the brittle plastic intake manifold levers and stop the peripheral oil leaks, the core rotating assembly will easily outlive the GLK's chassis and electronics.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. Delivers impeccably smooth, linear power with zero lag. It relies entirely on its large 3.5L displacement and a dual-stage variable intake manifold to generate a deep, torque-rich powerband.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch ME9.7. A reliable unit, but its Achilles heel is its physical location. Mounted directly flat on top of the hot intake manifold, it is subjected to massive heat cycling, which can eventually crack internal solder joints over a decade of use.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 5",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "300 hp. The bottom end is forged and massively over-engineered. However, because it is naturally aspirated, extracting power beyond a basic Stage 1 tune without forced induction is financially unjustifiable.",
