    "timingType": "Duplex timing chain. Mechanically similar to the standard M272, avoiding the earlier balance shaft issues. However, the addition of direct injection adds stress, so 10,000 km oil intervals remain mandatory.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI - Stratified Charge). This transitional engine uses highly complex, first-generation high-pressure piezo injectors spraying directly into the combustion chamber. While it bumps power to 292 hp, it introduces a host of catastrophic reliability issues including carbon buildup and injector failure.",
    "engineLifespan": "200 000 - 300 000 km. While the core block is the bulletproof M272, the direct injection peripherals (HPFP, Piezo injectors, NOX sensors) drastically lower the effective lifespan and significantly increase running costs compared to the standard 272 hp MPI version.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. Uses a variable resonance intake manifold. Delivers excellent throttle response and a strong top-end rush of power thanks to the higher 12.2:1 compression ratio.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.1. A highly complex direct-injection ECU managing the stratified lean-burn mode, multiple injection events, and NOX catalyst regeneration.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 5",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "330 hp. The bottom end is forged and can handle tuning, but the highly sensitive Piezo injectors and HPFP are the absolute limiting factors.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "13.5 - 15.0 L/100km",
      "highway": "8.0 - 9.5 L/100km",
      "mixed": "10.0 - 11.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "16.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.0L 5W-30 or 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5).",
    "commonIssues": [
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Wear: The mechanical pump driven by the camshaft wears internally, causing long cranks, lack of power, and an audible ticking noise.",
      "Direct Injection Carbon Buildup: Lack of port injection means oil vapors bake onto the intake valves, severely restricting airflow and causing rough idle after 80,000 km.",
      "NOX Sensor Failure: Engines operating in stratified charge mode burn very lean, causing high NOX emissions. The sensitive NOX sensors fail frequently, triggering a Check Engine Light.",
      "Piezo Injector Failure: Highly sensitive first-generation direct injectors can fail open, dumping fuel into the cylinder, causing misfires and severe risk to the engine block.",
      "Intake Manifold Tumble Flap Levers Breaking: Similar to the MPI M272, the plastic actuating levers on the front of the intake manifold become brittle and snap.",
      "Rear Camshaft Expansion Plugs Leaking: Round plastic plugs at the back of the cylinder heads shrink over time, leaking oil onto the hot exhaust.",
      "Thermostat Sticking Open: The thermostat commonly fails in the open position, preventing the engine from reaching operating temperature."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Cylinder Scoring (Injector Failure): A failed Piezo injector sticking open acts like a pressure washer, stripping the vital oil film off the cylinder wall and causing terminal scoring and engine destruction.",
      "HPFP Fuel Dilution: A severely failed high-pressure fuel pump can leak raw gasoline directly into the engine crankcase, diluting the oil and destroying all engine bearings instantly.",
      "Catastrophic Valvetrain Destruction via Carbon: If thick carbon buildup on the intake valves is ignored, the valves can fail to seat properly, leading to burnt valves and compression loss.",
      "ECU Heat Death: Mounted on top of the engine, the Bosch ECU can eventually suffer from heat death, causing random stalling or failure to start while driving.",
      "Conductor Plate Complete Failure (7G-Tronic): If the transmission fluid is neglected, the conductor plate fails completely, requiring a highly specialized repair.",
      "Catalyst Destruction from Stratified Lean-Burn Misfires: Driving with misfires caused by carbon buildup or failing Piezo injectors will superheat and melt the expensive catalytic converters."
    ],
