    "timingType": "Duplex timing chain (V6 at 60-degree angle). The M276 suffers from a notorious flaw with its secondary timing chain tensioners and a lack of check valves. This allows oil to drain back overnight, causing a terrifying metal-on-metal rattle on cold starts before oil pressure builds.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) operating at up to 200 Bar via advanced Piezo injectors. USA-spec models generally use a homogeneous fuel mixture map (rather than ultra-lean stratified charge) to comply with specific EPA regulations.",
    "engineLifespan": "250 000 - 350 000+ km. The 60-degree aluminum block is incredibly sturdy. Lifespan is heavily dictated by proactively installing the revised timing chain tensioners and check valves, as well as replacing the high-pressure fuel pump when it wears.",
    "turboType": "Naturally Aspirated. Uses a variable resonance intake manifold to maximize airflow across the RPM range, delivering peak torque efficiently without forced induction.",
