    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. A fundamentally compromised design choice. If the chain stretches due to extended oil intervals, replacing the chain and guides requires dropping the transmission or physically pulling the entire engine out of the chassis.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI). Uses highly reliable Delphi solenoid injectors directly from the factory, avoiding the Piezo disaster of the pre-facelift era. However, it features a highly complex Selective Catalytic Reduction (SCR / AdBlue) system injected directly into the exhaust stream to meet Euro 6 emissions.",
    "engineLifespan": "300 000 - 450 000+ km. The iron block and forged internals are virtually indestructible, but the practical lifespan of this specific BlueTEC variant is severely hindered by the fragile, overly complex, and incredibly expensive AdBlue/SCR emissions system.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbocharger (BorgWarner R2S). Uses a small high-pressure turbo for instant low-end response and a larger low-pressure turbo for mid-to-high RPM power. Provides an incredible 500 Nm of torque from just 1600 RPM with zero lag.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC17CP46. A highly complex Euro 6 system managing sequential turbo transitions, strict DPF regenerations, and continuous AdBlue dosing logic.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "280+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is massively over-engineered. The 204 hp factory output is extremely reliable, leaving strong headroom for aftermarket tuning.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "7.5 - 8.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "5.8 - 6.8 L/100km",
      "mixed": "6.5 - 7.5 L/100km",
      "sporty": "9.0+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.51 or MB 229.52).",
    "commonIssues": [
      "AdBlue Tank Heater Failure: The internal heating element in the AdBlue tank burns out, triggering a Check Engine Light and a dreaded 'Engine start not possible in 800 km' countdown.",
      "NOx Sensor Failure: Euro 6 models use highly sensitive NOx sensors that frequently fail due to soot and urea crystallization, requiring incredibly expensive replacements.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: Extended oil intervals cause the single-row rear timing chain to stretch. A rattling sound on cold starts is the first warning sign.",
      "Variable Oil Pump Solenoid Failure: The eco-focused variable oil pump control solenoid can stick, causing dangerously low oil pressure under load.",
      "Water Pump & Coolant Flange Leaks: The plastic water pump housing and the coolant connection pipe located under the fuel filter frequently crack and leak coolant slowly.",
      "Intake Manifold Swirl Flap Failure: Plastic linkages on the intake manifold wear out and break, causing boost leaks, terrible fuel economy, and Limp Mode.",
      "Sequential Turbo Vacuum Leaks: The vacuum transducers controlling the bypass flaps between the small and large turbos frequently fail or leak, causing erratic boost delivery."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Engine Seizure (Spun Bearings): If the variable oil pump solenoid fails in the 'low pressure' state during high engine load, the crankshaft main bearings will spin, destroying the engine block completely.",
      "SCR System Meltdown (No-Start Countdown): If any part of the AdBlue system fails (pump, heater, injector, NOx sensor), the ECU initiates a hard countdown. Once it reaches zero, the vehicle will permanently refuse to start until thousands of Euros are spent at the dealer.",
      "Timing Chain Jump / Valvetrain Destruction: Ignoring the cold-start chain rattle will eventually cause the stretched chain to skip a tooth on the camshaft sprockets, resulting in piston-to-valve contact.",
      "Engine-Out Maintenance Bill: Because the timing chain is mounted flush against the firewall, replacing it requires dropping the transmission or pulling the engine, resulting in an astronomical labor bill.",
      "Turbocharger Bearing Failure: Chronic DPF blockage creates massive exhaust backpressure, which prevents the twin turbos from spooling freely and quickly destroys their bearings.",
      "Conductor Plate Failure (7G-Tronic Plus): If the automatic transmission fluid is neglected, the immense 500 Nm of torque combined with metallic debris will destroy the delicate speed sensors inside the transmission conductor plate."
    ],
