    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. This is a fundamentally compromised design choice. If the chain stretches due to extended oil change intervals, replacing the chain and guides requires dropping the transmission or physically pulling the entire engine out of the chassis.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI). Uses highly reliable Delphi solenoid injectors. Features a complex Selective Catalytic Reduction (SCR / AdBlue) system mapped specifically for stringent North American Tier 2 Bin 5 emission regulations.",
    "engineLifespan": "200,000 - 300,000+ miles. The cast-iron block and forged internals are incredibly overbuilt and virtually indestructible. However, the practical lifespan of this specific US-spec BlueTEC is severely hindered by the fragile, overly complex, and incredibly expensive AdBlue/SCR system.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbocharger (BorgWarner R2S). Uses a small high-pressure turbo for instant low-end response and a larger low-pressure turbo for mid-to-high RPM power. Provides an incredible 369 lb-ft (500 Nm) of torque from just 1600 RPM with zero lag.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC17CP46. A highly complex system managing sequential turbo transitions and continuous AdBlue dosing logic. The USA-spec features highly aggressive DPF regeneration cycles and an unforgiving OBD-II diagnostic protocol.",
    "euroStandard": "Tier 2 Bin 5 (USA)",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "280+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is massively over-engineered. The 204 hp factory output is extremely reliable, leaving strong headroom for aftermarket tuning.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "24 - 26 mpg (US)",
      "highway": "32 - 34 mpg (US)",
      "mixed": "27 - 29 mpg (US)",
      "sporty": "21.0 mpg (US)"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.51 or MB 229.52 strictly required for US diesel quality).",
    "commonIssues": [
      "AdBlue Tank Heater Failure: The internal heating element in the DEF (AdBlue) tank burns out, triggering a Check Engine Light and an aggressive remaining starts countdown limit mandated by the EPA.",
      "NOx Sensor Failure: US models use highly sensitive NOx sensors that frequently fail due to soot and urea crystallization, requiring incredibly expensive replacements to clear the CEL.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Stretch: Extended oil intervals cause the single-row rear timing chain to stretch. A rattling sound on cold starts is the first warning sign.",
      "Variable Oil Pump Solenoid Failure: The eco-focused variable oil pump control solenoid can stick, causing dangerously low oil pressure under load.",
      "Water Pump & Coolant Flange Leaks: The plastic water pump housing and the coolant connection pipe located under the fuel filter frequently crack and leak coolant slowly.",
      "Intake Manifold Swirl Flap Failure: Plastic linkages on the intake manifold wear out and break, causing boost leaks, terrible fuel economy, and Limp Mode.",
      "DPF Pressure Sensor Failure: Highly aggressive US regeneration cycles frequently cook the differential pressure sensors, causing the ECU to lock out DPF regens entirely."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "SCR System Meltdown (X-Starts Remaining Countdown): If any part of the AdBlue system fails (pump, heater, injector, NOx sensor), the USA ECU initiates a strict 'Starts Remaining' countdown. Once it reaches zero, the vehicle is electronically bricked and will not crank until thousands of dollars are spent.",
      "Catastrophic Engine Seizure (Spun Bearings): If the variable oil pump solenoid fails in the 'low pressure' state during high engine load, the crankshaft main bearings will spin, destroying the engine block completely.",
      "Timing Chain Jump / Valvetrain Destruction: Ignoring the cold-start chain rattle will eventually cause the stretched chain to skip a tooth on the camshaft sprockets, resulting in piston-to-valve contact.",
      "Engine-Out Maintenance Bill: Because the timing chain is mounted flush against the firewall, replacing it requires dropping the transmission or pulling the engine, resulting in an astronomical labor bill.",
      "Turbocharger Bearing Failure: Chronic DPF blockage creates massive exhaust backpressure, which prevents the twin turbos from spooling freely and quickly destroys their bearings.",
      "Conductor Plate Failure (7G-Tronic Plus): If the automatic transmission fluid is neglected, the immense 500 Nm of torque combined with metallic debris will destroy the delicate speed sensors inside the transmission conductor plate."
    ],
