    "yearRange": "2009-2012",
    "timingType": "Duplex timing chain. Highly robust layout located at the front of the engine. Unlike the catastrophic 4-cylinder OM651, the V6's chain system rarely stretches before 300,000 km, and if it does, it is easily accessible without dropping the engine out of the chassis.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI). Utilizes highly reliable Bosch piezo-electric injectors operating at 1600 Bar. Far more reliable than early 4-cylinder diesels, though highly susceptible to 'Black Death' if the copper sealing washers fail and leak exhaust gases.",
    "engineLifespan": "400,000 - 600,000+ km. The OM642 is a legendary, overbuilt aluminum-block V6 diesel. If you proactively address the infamous oil cooler seals and keep the intake clear of oil, the core engine will easily outlast the GLK's chassis and electronics.",
    "turboType": "Single Garrett Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT). A highly reliable, massive turbocharger that provides a brutal wave of 540 Nm of torque. Susceptible to damage only if the inner lining of the factory exhaust manifolds break apart and send shrapnel into the turbine.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC16CP31. A very robust and highly tunable engine management system, utilizing a software-modified injection map compared to the older 320 CDI to optimize fuel delivery and squeeze out an extra 7 horsepower.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 5",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "320+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is incredibly strong. The factory 231 hp tune is a very conservative map, leaving immense potential for safe tuning without stressing the bottom end.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "9.0 - 10.5 L/100km",
      "highway": "6.8 - 7.8 L/100km",
      "mixed": "7.8 - 9.0 L/100km",
      "sporty": "11.5+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "8.5L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Low-SAPS (MB 229.51).",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Oil Cooler Seal Leak: The definitive OM642 issue. Factory orange viton seals on the oil cooler (buried deep in the 'V' of the engine) fail, causing a massive oil leak down the back of the engine block.",
      "Intake Port Shutoff Motor (M55) Short: The PCV system constantly drips oil directly into the turbo inlet seal. This oil drips down onto the M55 swirl flap motor, shorting it out and forcing the car into Limp Mode.",
      "Black Death (Injector Seal Failure): The copper crush washers sealing the injectors to the cylinder head fail, allowing exhaust gases to escape and bake into a hard, black, tar-like substance over the injectors.",
      "Exhaust Manifold Slag: The inner stainless-steel lining of the dual-wall exhaust manifolds can crack and break off over time. These metal shards fly directly into the turbocharger, destroying the turbine wheel.",
      "EGR & Intake Manifold Clogging: Heavy soot from the EGR mixes with oil vapor from the PCV, creating a thick, black sludge that severely chokes the intake manifolds and jams the swirl flaps.",
      "Glow Plug Module Failure: The solid-state glow plug control module frequently fails, causing cold start issues and a persistent Check Engine Light.",
      "Turbocharger Actuator Failure: The electronic actuator mounted on the side of the Garrett turbo burns out due to heat cycling, causing a complete loss of boost."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Oil Starvation: If the oil cooler seals fail completely and the leak is ignored, the engine will rapidly lose its 8.5 liters of oil while driving, seizing the main bearings.",
      "Turbocharger Destruction: Metal shards from degrading factory exhaust manifolds will instantly obliterate the turbocharger, requiring a highly expensive replacement.",
      "Cylinder Head Ruin ('Black Death'): If the injector seal leak is ignored for tens of thousands of kilometers, the injectors will become permanently welded into the cylinder head by baked carbon, requiring total head replacement.",
      "Conductor Plate Failure (7G-Tronic): The immense 540 Nm of torque puts significant strain on the transmission. Neglecting fluid changes guarantees the destruction of the conductor plate speed sensors.",
      "M55 Limp Mode Lockout: A shorted intake port shutoff motor will permanently lock the engine in Limp Mode (severely restricted power) until the intake manifolds are removed and the motor is replaced.",
      "DPF Thermal Runaway: If the car is driven exclusively in the city with a clogged EGR, the DPF will choke. Forced regenerations can cause extreme exhaust gas temperatures, potentially cracking the DPF housing."
    ],
