    "timingType": "Duplex timing chain. Located at the front of the engine. The OM 642 LS (Leistungssteigerung) variant retains the highly robust chain layout of the older generation, easily lasting well beyond 300,000 km. Replacement is straightforward without engine removal.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI). Features an upgraded high-pressure fuel pump and advanced piezo injectors operating at a massive 2000 Bar to support the 265 hp output. Highly reliable, but copper seal failure ('Black Death') remains a vital check.",
    "engineLifespan": "400,000 - 600,000+ km. The OM 642 LS is the ultimate evolution of this V6. The core block is practically immortal. Lifespan is dictated only by proactively managing the oil cooler seals, intake carbon buildup, and protecting the massive turbocharger.",
    "turboType": "Single Garrett Variable Nozzle Turbine (VNT). Upgraded specifically for the LS variant. Features a highly efficient compressor wheel and improved VNT vanes to handle the monumental 620 Nm of torque without suffering from lag.",
