    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain. Features Variable Valve Timing (VVT) on both intake and exhaust camshafts. The M274 has a notorious vulnerability regarding its intake camshaft adjuster locking pin, which frequently breaks and causes a loud cold-start metallic rattle.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) via high-pressure piezo injectors. Lacks port injection, making the intake valves highly susceptible to heavy carbon sludge buildup. US models have incredibly strict OBD-II monitors for misfires caused by this carbon.",
    "engineLifespan": "120,000 - 180,000+ miles. Lifespan is strictly dependent on abandoning the factory 10,000-mile oil change interval and doing it every 5,000 - 7,000 miles to protect the fragile VVT phasers and piston wrist-pins.",
    "turboType": "Single IHI Turbocharger with an electronic wastegate. Highly optimized factory mapping provides aggressive boost pressure to reach the US-certified 241 hp output.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17.7.2. Runs a heavily monitored SULEV (Super Ultra Low Emission Vehicle) software map, meaning any slight deviation in catalytic converter efficiency or fuel trim will trigger a Check Engine Light.",
