    "timingType": "Complex dual-stage timing chain system (primary and secondary chains). Unlike the early naturally aspirated M276 engines, the Biturbo variants have updated chain tensioners and check valves from the factory. The system is exceptionally reliable, typically lasting well over 250,000 km without stretching.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) via high-pressure piezo injectors operating up to 200 Bar. Very precise, though direct injection naturally leads to some carbon buildup on the intake valves over high mileage.",
    "engineLifespan": "250,000 - 350,000+ km. The M276 3.0L Biturbo is widely considered one of the most reliable and robust modern engines Mercedes-Benz has ever produced. The core aluminum block and forged rotating assembly are virtually bulletproof.",
