    "drivingExperience": "The GLC 43 AMG is the absolute sweet spot of the X253 lineup. The 3.0L Biturbo V6 fires up with a deep, menacing growl and delivers a massive wave of 520 Nm torque that makes the heavy SUV feel incredibly light and agile. The AMG-calibrated 9G-Tronic snaps through gears with aggressive throttle blips and produces loud, satisfying exhaust crackles on overrun in Sport+ mode. The rear-biased 4MATIC system (31:69) allows for playful, dynamic cornering, making it feel more like an elevated hot-hatch than a crossover. It perfectly blends brutal daily performance with refined Mercedes luxury.",
    "mechanicVerdict": "The M276 3.0L Biturbo in the GLC 43 AMG is a masterpiece of reliability, widely considered one of the most durable engines Mercedes has built in the last decade. Unlike the 4-cylinder models (M274) which suffer from catastrophic valvetrain failures, the M276's timing chain system is virtually bulletproof. The engine block and turbos easily outlast the vehicle if properly maintained. However, it has two specific flaws you MUST address. First, the upper timing covers leak oil; this is easily fixed by resealing them. Second, and crucially, the camshaft magnets can leak oil internally, sending it through the wiring harness directly into the ECU. You must inspect the connectors and install cheap, sacrificial 'pigtail' extension harnesses to block the oil. Do this, change the spark plugs every 40,000 km, and use good 5W-40 oil, and the engine is bulletproof. It earns a fantastic 4/10 risk rating.",
    "repairCostEstimate": "800 - 1,500 EUR / year",
