    "riskRating": 4,
    "drivingExperience": "The Facelift GLC 43 AMG elevates the driving experience to a completely new level. With the power bumped to 390 hp and larger turbos, it pulls significantly harder at the top end of the rev range compared to the pre-facelift model. The exhaust note is a fierce, menacing V6 howl. The real star, however, is the upgraded AMG Speedshift TCT 9G transmission logic; in Sport+ mode, gear changes are violently fast and accompanied by aggressive throttle blips and exhaust explosions. Combined with the rear-biased 4MATIC system, it is an outrageously fun, sporty, and highly practical daily driver.",
    "mechanicVerdict": "The M276 3.0L Biturbo in the Facelift GLC 43 AMG remains an absolute masterpiece of reliability. By completely avoiding the 48V mild-hybrid nonsense and sticking to raw, pure internal combustion, this 390 hp engine is arguably the most reliable powertrain in the entire X253 lineup. The timing chain system is virtually bulletproof, and the engine block will easily outlast the vehicle. However, it still retains two classic M276 flaws you MUST address. First, the upper timing covers leak oil; this is easily fixed by resealing them. Second, the camshaft magnets can leak oil internally, sending it through the wiring harness directly into the ECU. You must inspect the connectors and install cheap, sacrificial 'pigtail' extension harnesses to block the oil. Do this, change the spark plugs every 40,000 km, and use good 5W-40 oil, and you will have a flawless, high-performance SUV. It earns a fantastic 4/10 risk rating.",
    "repairCostEstimate": "800 - 1,500 EUR / year",
