      "MCT Transmission Destruction: The AMG SPEEDSHIFT MCT replaces the torque converter with a wet clutch. Continual aggressive launches will burn the clutch packs, requiring a highly specialized and expensive rebuild.",
      "Cylinder Washout via Injector Failure: A stuck-open direct injector will wash the protective oil film off the Nanoslide cylinder walls, causing terminal block damage within minutes.",
      "Engine Wiring Harness Meltdown: The 'Hot-V' turbochargers act as an oven for the engine valley. High mileage causes plastic vacuum lines and wiring insulation to turn brittle and shatter.",
      "Exhaust Actuator Seizure: The electronic motors controlling the variable exhaust flaps seize. Integrated into the CAN-bus, their failure can occasionally trigger Limp Mode.",
      "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) Roller Wear: The camshaft-driven rollers on the twin HPFPs wear down under high loads, eventually sending metallic shrapnel into the fuel system."
