    "timingType": "Simplex/Duplex chain combination. The timing drive system on the M177 is exceptionally robust, mounted at the front of the engine, and utilizes massive tensioners. Timing chain stretch or failure is virtually unheard of on this V8.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (CGI) featuring highly precise Bosch piezo injectors. Lacks port injection, but the advanced crankcase ventilation system helps delay heavy carbon sludge buildup on the intake valves.",
    "engineLifespan": "250,000 - 350,000+ km. The core aluminum closed-deck block with Nanoslide cylinder coating is incredibly durable. However, the lifespan is heavily dictated by proactive peripheral maintenance—specifically monitoring the PCV system to prevent catastrophic Rear Main Seal (RMS) blowouts.",
    "turboType": "Twin BorgWarner Twin-Scroll Turbochargers mounted inside the 'V' of the engine block (Hot-V configuration). The 'S' variant features fully unlocked boost mapping, providing incredibly responsive, lag-free torque delivery, but concentrates a massive amount of heat directly under the hood.",
