    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block against the firewall. This is the OM651's most critical design flaw. If the chain stretches due to extended 25,000 km oil intervals, replacing the chain and guides requires dropping the transmission or pulling the entire engine out of the chassis.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI). Utilizes highly reliable Delphi solenoid injectors. Far less problematic than the early piezo injectors used on the previous W204 generation OM651 engines.",
    "engineLifespan": "300,000 - 500,000+ km. The heavy cast-iron block and forged rotating assembly are legendary for their brute, commercial-grade strength. However, reaching high mileage requires proactive timing chain replacement and permanently fixing the oil pump solenoid flaw.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbocharger (BorgWarner R2S). A small high-pressure turbo provides instant response off the line, while a larger low-pressure turbo takes over at higher RPMs. Produces a massive 500 Nm of torque with virtually zero lag.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch EDC17. A highly tunable and robust engine management system. On the 250 d, the ECU runs the fully unlocked factory software map for the OM651 series, maximizing boost and fueling.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "280+ hp. The internal rotating assembly is massively over-engineered. The 204 hp output is standard for this hardware, leaving immense headroom for aftermarket tuning without stressing the bottom end.",
