    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. While incredibly durable compared to older V6s, its location against the firewall means that if replacement is ever required, the transmission must be dropped or the engine removed.",
    "injectionType": "Common Rail Direct Injection (CRDI) via Bosch Piezo injectors operating at an immense 2,500 Bar. Features stepped-bowl combustion chambers in the steel pistons for highly efficient, low-soot burning.",
    "engineLifespan": "300,000 - 500,000+ km. The OM656 Inline-6 is an absolute masterpiece of modern engineering. The core block (aluminum with steel pistons) is virtually indestructible. Lifespan is primarily threatened by peripheral emissions components and a specific factory coolant valve flaw.",
    "turboType": "Sequential Twin-Turbocharger (Biturbo). Utilizes a smaller high-pressure turbo for instant low-end response and a larger low-pressure turbo for top-end breathing. Produces a devastating 700 Nm of torque effortlessly.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MD1. A highly advanced engine management system. On the 400 d, it runs the fully unlocked, maximum-output factory map, integrating seamlessly with the Camtronic exhaust valve lift system.",
