    "oilSpecification": "8.0L 5W-30 Fully Synthetic Ultra Low-SAPS (MB 229.52). 0W-20 is often used from the factory for emissions, but high-quality 5W-30 is strongly recommended by mechanics to protect the valvetrain and twin turbos under the heavy 330 hp load.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "Coolant Valve Vacuum Leak: The most notorious flaw shared with the OM654. The coolant shut-off valve leaks internally, pushing coolant directly into the vacuum system lines, destroying the vacuum pump and brake booster.",
      "Camshaft Rocker Arm Wear: Using 0W-20 oil over extended 25,000 km intervals can cause premature wear on the roller rocker arm bearings, especially under the 400d's thermal load.",
      "NOx Sensor Failure: The dual NOx sensors fail frequently due to urea crystallization or soot, triggering an immediate Check Engine Light.",
      "AdBlue Injector Clogging: The AdBlue dosing nozzle crystalizes and clogs, preventing DEF injection and triggering the no-start countdown.",
      "Tandem Oil Pump Valve Sticking: The variable oil pump solenoid can stick, causing low oil pressure warnings.",
      "DPF Pressure Sensor Failure: Condensation ruins the DPF differential pressure sensor, preventing active regenerations."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "Catastrophic Brake Booster Failure (Coolant Leak): If the coolant shut-off valve fails and pushes coolant through the vacuum lines, it will flood the vacuum pump and brake booster, leading to a sudden loss of braking assistance and a 2,000+ EUR repair bill.",
      "AdBlue / SCR System Meltdown (Countdown): If any component of the complex Euro 6d AdBlue system fails, the ECU initiates a strict 'Starts Remaining' countdown. Once zero is reached, the car electronically bricks itself.",
      "Engine-Out Maintenance Bill: Because the timing chain is mounted flush against the firewall, replacing a stretched chain requires dropping the transmission or pulling the engine.",
      "Valvetrain Destruction (Rocker Arms): If the roller rocker arms fail due to thin 0W-20 oil and the noise is ignored, they will grind the camshaft lobes down to bare metal.",
      "Fuel System Shrapnel: Operating at 2,500 Bar, the Bosch fuel pump is highly sensitive. Contaminated fuel will destroy it rapidly, sending metallic shrapnel through the entire fuel system.",
      "DPF Thermal Cracking: Repeated, failed DPF regenerations caused by city driving will cause the DPF core to melt or crack, requiring a hugely expensive replacement.",
      "Conductor Plate Failure (9G-Tronic): Neglecting the 80,000 km transmission fluid service will allow metallic debris to short out the sensitive internal solenoids."
    ],
