      "Rear Timing Chain Replacement: Because the timing chain is mounted flush against the firewall, replacing a stretched chain requires dropping the transmission or pulling the engine—a massive labor expense.",
      "Conicshape Cylinder Wear: The engine uses 'trumpet-honing' (cylinders are wider at the bottom). If the incredibly thin 0W-20 oil is not changed frequently (10,000 km), this specialized honing can wear prematurely under high loads.",
      "Electronic Water Pump Failure: The cooling system relies on highly complex electronic valves and pumps that are prone to sudden failure, risking rapid engine overheating.",
      "GPF Thermal Cracking: Constant short trips prevent the GPF from regenerating. Eventually, the filter core can crack or melt due to thermal stress.",
      "Direct Injector Sticking: The 350-bar piezo injectors can fail due to carbon buildup or poor fuel quality, washing the cylinder walls with raw fuel and destroying the Nanoslide coating."
