    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the engine block. Mercedes moved the chain to the transmission side to improve pedestrian safety and NVH. While mechanically robust, replacing it requires dropping the transmission or pulling the engine out.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection with a 350 Bar high-pressure fuel system. Uses advanced piezo injectors for highly precise fuel delivery. North American models are calibrated for lower US octane standards (91 AKI minimum).",
    "engineLifespan": "150,000 - 200,000+ Miles (Internal Combustion Engine). The core aluminum block is highly advanced and resolves the catastrophic piston-cracking issues of the older M274. However, the true lifespan of the vehicle is dictated by the highly complex 48V electrical system and the Integrated Starter-Generator (ISG).",
    "turboType": "Twin-Scroll Turbocharger engineered closely with the Mercedes-AMG Formula 1 team. Paired with a 48V Integrated Starter-Generator (ISG) that provides 200 Nm of instant electrical torque to completely mask any turbo lag.",
