    "timingType": "Simplex timing chain located at the REAR of the internal combustion engine (ICE). Extremely durable, but requires engine or transmission removal if replacement is needed.",
    "injectionType": "Direct Injection (350 Bar) for the ICE. Electric propulsion is handled by a massive 100 kW (136 hp) permanently excited synchronous electric motor integrated into the transmission bellhousing.",
    "engineLifespan": "200,000 - 300,000+ km (ICE component). The core M254 aluminum block is virtually indestructible. However, the lifespan of the vehicle as a whole is severely threatened by high-voltage battery degradation (specifically the massive 31.2 kWh pack), On-Board Charger (OBC) failures, and the extreme stress the ~2,400 kg kerb weight places on the chassis.",
    "turboType": "Twin-Scroll Turbocharger. The 100 kW electric motor provides 440 Nm of instant, zero-lag torque from a standstill, completely masking any petrol turbo lag and delivering explosive low-end acceleration.",
    "ecuType": "Bosch MED17 / MD1 variant tightly integrated with the High-Voltage Battery Management System (BMS) and hybrid power electronics. Highly complex, proprietary software architecture.",
    "euroStandard": "Euro 6e / Euro 6d-ISC-FCM",
    "maxPowerStockInternals": "370+ hp (Combined). The 204 hp petrol engine is artificially detuned and can easily be mapped to ~260 hp. When combined with the 136 hp electric motor, total system output can safely exceed 370 hp and 650 Nm without altering the hardware.",
    "fuelConsumption": {
      "city": "0.5 - 1.5 L/100km (with charged battery)",
      "highway": "7.5 - 8.5 L/100km (battery depleted)",
      "mixed": "1.5 - 6.5 L/100km (highly dependent on charging habits)",
      "sporty": "10.5+ L/100km"
    },
    "oilSpecification": "6.0L 0W-20 Fully Synthetic Ultra Low-SAPS (MB 229.71). Factory fill is designed for maximum efficiency. However, because the ICE engine suffers sudden high-RPM cold starts when the battery dies on the highway, independent mechanics strongly advise using 5W-30 (MB 229.52) for vastly superior hydrodynamic protection.",
    "commonIssues": [
      "DC Fast Charging Thermal Stress: The optional 60 kW DC fast charger degrades the 31.2 kWh lithium-ion battery rapidly if used frequently, causing premature capacity loss.",
      "On-Board Charger (OBC) Failure: The internal 11 kW AC charger fails, preventing the high-voltage battery from being charged via a wall plug or public Type 2 station.",
      "HV Battery Cooling Circuit Leaks: The high-voltage battery relies on the A/C refrigerant loop to stay cool. Leaks in this system overheat the battery and trigger hybrid system shutdowns.",
      "Air Suspension Collapse: The extreme weight of the vehicle (nearly 2.4 tons) obliterates the rear air suspension bags and burns out the compressor prematurely.",
      "GPF Clogging: Because the electric motor handles city driving, the petrol engine rarely reaches operating temperature during short trips, leading to soot accumulation and blocked Gasoline Particulate Filters.",
      "Camshaft Valvetrain Wear (ICE): Frequent cold-starting of the petrol engine under heavy load (when the battery suddenly depletes) causes premature wear on the valvetrain."
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      "High-Voltage Battery Degradation: The 31.2 kWh lithium-ion battery is massive for a PHEV. If it degrades, replacement costs are astronomical (15,000+ EUR), and the car is left dragging around 400 kg of dead weight, ruining fuel economy.",
      "OBC / Inverter Death: Failure of the high-voltage power electronics often requires replacing the entire modular unit at the cost of 4,000 - 6,000 EUR out of warranty.",
      "Massive Hybrid Motor Labor Cost: The 100 kW electric motor is sandwiched between the engine and the 9G-Tronic transmission. If it fails mechanically or electrically, the entire transmission must be dropped.",
      "Rear Timing Chain Replacement: Because the timing chain is mounted flush against the firewall, replacing a stretched chain requires dropping the transmission or pulling the engine.",
      "Electronic Water Pump Failure (ICE): The ICE cooling system relies on highly complex electronic valves and pumps that are prone to sudden failure.",
      "Hybrid Clutch Shudder: The wet clutch separating the electric motor from the ICE can shudder or slip if transmission fluid maintenance is neglected, leading to violent jerks during ICE engagement.",
      "Braking System Overload: The extreme weight of the vehicle easily overwhelms the standard braking system during spirited driving, leading to warped rotors and boiled brake fluid."
    ],
