    "author": ".",
    "riskRating": 8,
    "drivingExperience": "The GLC 300 de is an absolute torque monster. Combining a smooth diesel engine with a massive 100 kW electric motor yields a staggering 750 Nm of system torque from zero RPM. When driving on electricity, it is whisper-quiet and effortlessly smooth for over 100 km. When you accelerate hard or the battery depletes, the diesel engine kicks in seamlessly. The massive torque wave makes overtaking heavy traffic effortless. However, weighing nearly 2.4 tons due to the enormous 31.2 kWh battery, it feels heavy under hard braking and sharp cornering.",
    "mechanicVerdict": "The GLC 300 de is a technological marvel that combines the worst maintenance nightmares of modern diesels and complex plug-in hybrids. Mechanically, you have the robust OM654M diesel block, but it suffers from brutal cold-starts under load when the battery depletes on the highway. You MUST change the oil every 10,000 km with 5W-30 and change the fuel filter every 30,000 km to protect the CP4 pump.\n\nElectrically and environmentally, it is a ticking time bomb. The car relies on electric power in the city, meaning the diesel engine rarely reaches operating temperature, rapidly clogging the DPF and EGR valves—you must take it on weekly highway runs. Furthermore, the massive 31.2 kWh battery adds extreme weight that destroys rear air suspension and overburdens brakes, and On-Board Charger (OBC) failures are common out of warranty. It earns an 8/10 risk rating.",
    "repairCostEstimate": "2,000 - 4,500 EUR / year",
